<tbody id="A4.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 4\delta^{2/3}\mathsf{TV}(b,b^{\prime})\left\lVert\frac{b}{b^{\prime}}\right\rVert_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>b</mi><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 4\delta^{2/3}\mathsf{TV}(b,b^{\prime})\left\lVert\frac{b}{b^{\prime}}\right\rVert_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p7.5" class="ltx_p">where the second equality is by <a href="#A4.Thmlemma1" title="Lemma D.1. ‣ D.1 Belief Contraction ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>; the first inequality bounds each term <math id="A4.SS1.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{B}_{h}(b;x),\mathbb{B}_{h}(b^{\prime};x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{B}_{h}(b;x),\mathbb{B}_{h}(b^{\prime};x))</annotation></semantics></math> using <a href="#A4.E6" title="In D.1 Belief Contraction ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eqs.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, <a href="#A4.E7" title="Equation 7 ‣ D.1 Belief Contraction ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> and <a href="#A4.E8" title="Equation 8 ‣ D.1 Belief Contraction ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>; the second inequality uses the definition of <math id="A4.SS1.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math>; and the final inequality uses the data processing inequality for kernels <math id="A4.SS1.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{O}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕆</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{O}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>. Additionally,</p>
<table id="A4.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr[x\not\in\mathcal{E}]=\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{h}\setminus\mathcal{E}}\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}b)=\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{h}}\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}b)\mathbbm{1}\left[\frac{\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}b)}{E_{h}(x\mid{}b)}&lt;\delta^{1/3}\right]\leq\delta^{1/3}\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{h}}E_{h}(x\mid{}b)=\delta^{1/3}\addcontentsline{lla}{section}{\hbox to20.74pt{\crtrefnumber{eq:xi-bad-set}\hfil}eq:xi-bad-set}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∖</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mi>𝕆</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></munder><msub><mi>𝕆</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝕆</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></munder><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr[x\not\in\mathcal{E}]=\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{h}\setminus\mathcal{E}}\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}b)=\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{h}}\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}b)\mathbbm{1}\left[\frac{\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}b)}{E_{h}(x\mid{}b)}&lt;\delta^{1/3}\right]\leq\delta^{1/3}\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{h}}E_{h}(x\mid{}b)=\delta^{1/3}\addcontentsline{lla}{section}{\hbox to20.74pt{\crtrefnumber{eq:xi-bad-set}\hfil}eq:xi-bad-set}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p7.6" class="ltx_p">since <math id="A4.SS1.p7.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="E_{h}(\cdot\mid{}b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{h}(\cdot\mid{}b)</annotation></semantics></math> is a distribution. It follows that</p>
<table id="A4.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex97"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex97.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr\left[\xi&gt;4\delta^{1/3}\mathsf{TV}(b,b^{\prime})\left\lVert\frac{b}{b^{\prime}}\right\rVert_{\infty}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>b</mi><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr\left[\xi&gt;4\delta^{1/3}\mathsf{TV}(b,b^{\prime})\left\lVert\frac{b}{b^{\prime}}\right\rVert_{\infty}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex97.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\Pr\left[\xi\mathbbm{1}[x\in\mathcal{E}]&gt;4\delta^{1/3}\mathsf{TV}(b,b^{\prime})\left\lVert\frac{b}{b^{\prime}}\right\rVert_{\infty}\right]+\Pr[x\not\in\mathcal{E}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>b</mi><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\Pr\left[\xi\mathbbm{1}[x\in\mathcal{E}]&gt;4\delta^{1/3}\mathsf{TV}(b,b^{\prime})\left\lVert\frac{b}{b^{\prime}}\right\rVert_{\infty}\right]+\Pr[x\not\in\mathcal{E}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex98"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex98.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\delta^{1/3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\delta^{1/3}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p7.7" class="ltx_p">where the second inequality applies Markov’s inequality to <a href="#A4.E9" title="In D.1 Belief Contraction ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> for the first term, and <a href="#A4.E10" title="In D.1 Belief Contraction ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> for the second term. This proves the second claim of the lemma statement. To prove the first claim, note that <math id="A4.SS1.p7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{h}(x\mid{}b)\leq\delta^{-1}\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕆</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{h}(x\mid{}b)\leq\delta^{-1}\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}b)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A4.SS1.p7.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{X}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{X}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, modifying the calculation from <a href="#A4.E9" title="In D.1 Belief Contraction ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> (this time summing over all <math id="A4.SS1.p7.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{X}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{X}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> instead of <math id="A4.SS1.p7.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math>) gives</p>
<table id="A4.Ex99" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex99.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\xi]=\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{h}}\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}b)\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{B}_{h}(b;x),\mathbb{B}_{h}(b^{\prime};x))\left\lVert\frac{\mathbb{B}(b;x)}{\mathbb{B}(b^{\prime};x)}\right\rVert_{\infty}\leq 4\mathsf{TV}(b,b^{\prime})\left\lVert\frac{b}{b^{\prime}}\right\rVert_{\infty}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>𝕆</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mfrac><mi>b</mi><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mfrac><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\xi]=\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{h}}\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}b)\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{B}_{h}(b;x),\mathbb{B}_{h}(b^{\prime};x))\left\lVert\frac{\mathbb{B}(b;x)}{\mathbb{B}(b^{\prime};x)}\right\rVert_{\infty}\leq 4\mathsf{TV}(b,b^{\prime})\left\lVert\frac{b}{b^{\prime}}\right\rVert_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p7.8" class="ltx_p">as needed.
∎
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">The following result, which shows that the error metric decays with high probability under a belief update, is straightforward consequence of <a href="#A4.Thmlemma2" title="Lemma D.2. ‣ D.1 Belief Contraction ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a> and the data processing inequality.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmcorollary1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmcorollary1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary D.1</span></span><span id="A4.Thmcorollary1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmcorollary1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.Thmcorollary1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fix <math id="A4.Thmcorollary1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in\{2,\dots,H\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in\{2,\dots,H\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A4.Thmcorollary1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b,b^{\prime}\in\Delta(\mathcal{S}_{h-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b,b^{\prime}\in\Delta(\mathcal{S}_{h-1})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.Thmcorollary1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\ll b^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≪</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\ll b^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. For any action <math id="A4.Thmcorollary1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{h-1}\in\mathcal{A}_{h-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{h-1}\in\mathcal{A}_{h-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, with expectation over <math id="A4.Thmcorollary1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{h}\sim(\mathbb{O}_{h})^{\top}\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})\cdot b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝕆</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{h}\sim(\mathbb{O}_{h})^{\top}\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})\cdot b</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A4.Ex100" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex100.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}[D_{\star}(\mathbb{U}_{h}(b;a_{h-1},x_{h})\|\mathbb{U}_{h}(b^{\prime};a_{h-1},x_{h}))]\leq 4D_{\star}(b\|b^{\prime})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝕌</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝕌</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>D</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[D_{\star}(\mathbb{U}_{h}(b;a_{h-1},x_{h})\|\mathbb{U}_{h}(b^{\prime};a_{h-1},x_{h}))]\leq 4D_{\star}(b\|b^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmcorollary1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A4.Ex101" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex101.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr[D_{\star}(\mathbb{U}_{h}(b;a_{h-1},x_{h})\|\mathbb{U}_{h}(b^{\prime};a_{h-1},x_{h}))&gt;4\delta^{1/3}D_{\star}(b\|b^{\prime})]\leq 2\delta^{1/3}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝕌</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝕌</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>D</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr[D_{\star}(\mathbb{U}_{h}(b;a_{h-1},x_{h})\|\mathbb{U}_{h}(b^{\prime};a_{h-1},x_{h}))&gt;4\delta^{1/3}D_{\star}(b\|b^{\prime})]\leq 2\delta^{1/3}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof. </span>By applying <a href="#A4.Thmlemma2" title="Lemma D.2. ‣ D.1 Belief Contraction ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a> with <math id="A4.SS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})\cdot b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})\cdot b</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})\cdot b^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})\cdot b^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A4.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex102"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex102.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[D_{\star}(\mathbb{U}_{h}(b;a_{h-1},x_{h})\|\mathbb{U}_{h}(b^{\prime};a_{h-1},x_{h}))]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝕌</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝕌</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[D_{\star}(\mathbb{U}_{h}(b;a_{h-1},x_{h})\|\mathbb{U}_{h}(b^{\prime};a_{h-1},x_{h}))]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex102.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x_{h}\sim(\mathbb{O}_{h})^{\top}\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})\cdot b}[D_{\star}(\mathbb{B}_{h}(\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})\cdot b;x_{h})\|\mathbb{B}_{h}(\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})\cdot b^{\prime};x_{h}))]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝕆</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x_{h}\sim(\mathbb{O}_{h})^{\top}\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})\cdot b}[D_{\star}(\mathbb{B}_{h}(\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})\cdot b;x_{h})\|\mathbb{B}_{h}(\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})\cdot b^{\prime};x_{h}))]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex103"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex103.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 4D_{\star}(\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})\cdot b\|\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})\cdot b^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>D</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 4D_{\star}(\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})\cdot b\|\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})\cdot b^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex104"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex104.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 4D_{\star}(b\|b^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>D</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 4D_{\star}(b\|b^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p9.2" class="ltx_p">where the final inequality uses the fact that <math id="A4.SS1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{T}_{h}(a)\cdot b,\mathbb{T}_{h}(a)\cdot b^{\prime})\leq\mathsf{TV}(b,b^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝕋</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝕋</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{T}_{h}(a)\cdot b,\mathbb{T}_{h}(a)\cdot b^{\prime})\leq\mathsf{TV}(b,b^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lVert\frac{\mathbb{T}_{h}(a)\cdot b}{\mathbb{T}_{h}(a)\cdot b^{\prime}}\right\rVert_{\infty}\leq\left\lVert\frac{b}{b^{\prime}}\right\rVert_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝕋</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝕋</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mfrac><mi>b</mi><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mfrac><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lVert\frac{\mathbb{T}_{h}(a)\cdot b}{\mathbb{T}_{h}(a)\cdot b^{\prime}}\right\rVert_{\infty}\leq\left\lVert\frac{b}{b^{\prime}}\right\rVert_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> by the data processing inequality (<a href="#A3.Thmlemma1" title="Lemma C.1 (Data processing inequality). ‣ Appendix C Technical Lemmas ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>). Similarly, the second claim of <a href="#A4.Thmlemma2" title="Lemma D.2. ‣ D.1 Belief Contraction ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a> gives that</p>
<table id="A4.Ex105" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex105.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr\left[D_{\star}(\mathbb{U}_{h}(b;a_{h-1},x_{h})\|\mathbb{U}_{h}(b^{\prime};a_{h-1},x_{h}))&gt;4\delta^{1/3}D_{\star}(\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})\cdot b\|\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})\cdot b^{\prime})\right]\leq 2\delta^{1/3}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝕌</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝕌</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>D</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\left[D_{\star}(\mathbb{U}_{h}(b;a_{h-1},x_{h})\|\mathbb{U}_{h}(b^{\prime};a_{h-1},x_{h}))&gt;4\delta^{1/3}D_{\star}(\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})\cdot b\|\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})\cdot b^{\prime})\right]\leq 2\delta^{1/3}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p9.3" class="ltx_p">and therefore</p>
<table id="A4.Ex106" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex106.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr\left[D_{\star}(\mathbb{U}_{h}(b;a_{h-1},x_{h})\|\mathbb{U}_{h}(b^{\prime};a_{h-1},x_{h}))&gt;4\delta^{1/3}D_{\star}(b\|b^{\prime})\right]\leq 2\delta^{1/3}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝕌</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝕌</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>D</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\left[D_{\star}(\mathbb{U}_{h}(b;a_{h-1},x_{h})\|\mathbb{U}_{h}(b^{\prime};a_{h-1},x_{h}))&gt;4\delta^{1/3}D_{\star}(b\|b^{\prime})\right]\leq 2\delta^{1/3}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p9.4" class="ltx_p">by again applying the data processing inequality as above.
∎
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">We now can prove our main belief contraction result (which includes <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 3.2 (See ). ‣ 3.3 The Perturbed Block MDP ‣ 3 Approximate Decodability and Belief Contraction ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a> as a special case) by iteratively applying <a href="#A4.Thmcorollary1" title="Corollary D.1. ‣ D.1 Belief Contraction ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Corollary</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>. The main technical detail is to verify that the observations are indeed drawn from the true belief states, which relies on <a href="#A3.Thmlemma2" title="Lemma C.2. ‣ Appendix C Technical Lemmas ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem D.1</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There is a universal constant <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\ref{thm:belief-contraction}}&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem D.1. ‣ D.1 Belief Contraction ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a></mtext></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\ref{thm:belief-contraction}}&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> with the following property. Fix an executable policy <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>, indices <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq h&lt;h+L\leq H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq h&lt;h+L\leq H</annotation></semantics></math>, and distributions <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D},\mathcal{D}^{\prime}\in\Delta(\mathcal{S}_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D},\mathcal{D}^{\prime}\in\Delta(\mathcal{S}_{h})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then for any partial history <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})</annotation></semantics></math> it holds that</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex107" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex107.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{s_{h}\sim\mathcal{D}^{\prime}}\mathbb{E}^{\pi}[\mathsf{TV}(\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h+L}(x_{h+1:h+L},a_{h:h+L-1};\mathcal{D}^{\prime}),\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h+L}(x_{h+1:h+L},a_{h:h+L-1};\mathcal{D}))\mid{}s_{h}]\leq(C_{\ref{thm:belief-contraction}}\delta)^{L/9}\left\lVert\frac{\mathcal{D}^{\prime}}{\mathcal{D}}\right\rVert_{\infty}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐛</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mi>𝖺𝗉𝗑</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐛</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mi>𝖺𝗉𝗑</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem D.1. ‣ D.1 Belief Contraction ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a></mtext></msub><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mfrac><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mfrac><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{s_{h}\sim\mathcal{D}^{\prime}}\mathbb{E}^{\pi}[\mathsf{TV}(\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h+L}(x_{h+1:h+L},a_{h:h+L-1};\mathcal{D}^{\prime}),\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h+L}(x_{h+1:h+L},a_{h:h+L-1};\mathcal{D}))\mid{}s_{h}]\leq(C_{\ref{thm:belief-contraction}}\delta)^{L/9}\left\lVert\frac{\mathcal{D}^{\prime}}{\mathcal{D}}\right\rVert_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the inner expectation is over partial trajectories <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(x_{h+1:h+L},a_{h:h+L-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{h+1:h+L},a_{h:h+L-1})</annotation></semantics></math> drawn from policy <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> with the environment initialized in state <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> at step <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">As a consequence, it holds for any partial history <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})</annotation></semantics></math> that</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex108" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex108.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}^{\pi}[\mathsf{TV}(\mathbf{b}_{h+L}(x_{1:h+L},a_{1:h+L-1}),\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h+L}(x_{h+1:h+L},a_{h:h+L-1};\mathcal{D}))]\leq(C_{\ref{thm:belief-contraction}}\delta)^{L/9}\left\lVert\frac{\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})}{\mathcal{D}}\right\rVert_{\infty}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐛</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mi>𝖺𝗉𝗑</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem D.1. ‣ D.1 Belief Contraction ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a></mtext></msub><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝐛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mfrac><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}^{\pi}[\mathsf{TV}(\mathbf{b}_{h+L}(x_{1:h+L},a_{1:h+L-1}),\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h+L}(x_{h+1:h+L},a_{h:h+L-1};\mathcal{D}))]\leq(C_{\ref{thm:belief-contraction}}\delta)^{L/9}\left\lVert\frac{\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})}{\mathcal{D}}\right\rVert_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the expectation is over trajectories drawn from <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> conditioned on the partial history <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof. </span>We first observe that the second claim follows from the first claim by setting <math id="A4.SS1.p11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{D}^{\prime}:=\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}^{\prime}:=\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})</annotation></semantics></math>. Indeed, conditioned on <math id="A4.SS1.p11.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})</annotation></semantics></math>, the law of <math id="A4.SS1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> is precisely <math id="A4.SS1.p11.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#A3.Thmlemma2" title="Lemma C.2. ‣ Appendix C Technical Lemmas ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>), so drawing <math id="A4.SS1.p11.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(x_{h+1:h+L},a_{h:h+L-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{h+1:h+L},a_{h:h+L-1})</annotation></semantics></math> conditioned on <math id="A4.SS1.p11.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent to first drawing <math id="A4.SS1.p11.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="s_{h}\sim\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{h}\sim\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})</annotation></semantics></math> and then drawing <math id="A4.SS1.p11.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(x_{h+1:h+L},a_{h:h+L-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{h+1:h+L},a_{h:h+L-1})</annotation></semantics></math> from the POMDP initialized at <math id="A4.SS1.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, by the recursive definitions of <math id="A4.SS1.p11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐛</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{b}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>𝖺𝗉𝗑</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A4.Ex109" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex109.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{b}_{h+L}(x_{1:h+L},a_{1:h+L-1})=\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h+L}(x_{h+1:h+L},a_{h:h+L-1};\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1}))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐛</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mi>𝖺𝗉𝗑</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{b}_{h+L}(x_{1:h+L},a_{1:h+L-1})=\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h+L}(x_{h+1:h+L},a_{h:h+L-1};\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p12.1" class="ltx_p">It remains to prove the first claim. Fix <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq t\leq L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq t\leq L</annotation></semantics></math>, define the random variable</p>
<table id="A4.Ex110" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex110.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="X_{t}:=4^{-t}D_{\star}(\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h+t}(x_{h+1:h+t},a_{h:h+t-1};\mathcal{D}^{\prime})\|\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h+t}(x_{h+1:h+t},a_{h:h+t-1};\mathcal{D}))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>D</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐛</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>𝖺𝗉𝗑</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐛</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>𝖺𝗉𝗑</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}:=4^{-t}D_{\star}(\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h+t}(x_{h+1:h+t},a_{h:h+t-1};\mathcal{D}^{\prime})\|\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h+t}(x_{h+1:h+t},a_{h:h+t-1};\mathcal{D}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p12.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(x_{h+1:h+L},a_{h:h+L-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{h+1:h+L},a_{h:h+L-1})</annotation></semantics></math> is drawn by sampling <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{h}\sim\mathcal{D}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{h}\sim\mathcal{D}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, initializing the POMDP at <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, and then rolling out with policy <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> (to be precise, the action distribution at step <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h+t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h+t</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi(x_{1:h+t},a_{1:h+t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(x_{1:h+t},a_{1:h+t-1})</annotation></semantics></math>). Note that the roll-out does not resample <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is already fixed. Recall that <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\star}(p\|q):=\mathsf{TV}(p,q)\left\lVert\frac{p}{q}\right\rVert_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mi>q</mi></mfrac><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\star}(p\|q):=\mathsf{TV}(p,q)\left\lVert\frac{p}{q}\right\rVert_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>, so that <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(p,q)\leq D_{\star}(p\|q)\leq\left\lVert\frac{p}{q}\right\rVert_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mi>q</mi></mfrac><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(p,q)\leq D_{\star}(p\|q)\leq\left\lVert\frac{p}{q}\right\rVert_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> for any distributions <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p,q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,q</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</p>
<table id="A4.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex111"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex111.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=D_{\star}(\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h}(\emptyset;\mathcal{D}^{\prime})\|\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h}(\emptyset;\mathcal{D}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>𝖺𝗉𝗑</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>𝖺𝗉𝗑</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo>;</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=D_{\star}(\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h}(\emptyset;\mathcal{D}^{\prime})\|\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h}(\emptyset;\mathcal{D}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex112"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex112.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=D_{\star}(\mathcal{D}^{\prime}\|\mathcal{D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=D_{\star}(\mathcal{D}^{\prime}\|\mathcal{D})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex113"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex113.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left\lVert\frac{\mathcal{D}^{\prime}}{\mathcal{D}}\right\rVert_{\infty}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left\lVert\frac{\mathcal{D}^{\prime}}{\mathcal{D}}\right\rVert_{\infty}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p12.3" class="ltx_p">Moreover,</p>
<table id="A4.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex114"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex114.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{TV}(\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h+L}(x_{h+1:h+L},a_{h:h+L-1};\mathcal{D}^{\prime}),\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h+L}(x_{h+1:h+L},a_{h:h+L-1};\mathcal{D}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐛</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mi>𝖺𝗉𝗑</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐛</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mi>𝖺𝗉𝗑</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{TV}(\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h+L}(x_{h+1:h+L},a_{h:h+L-1};\mathcal{D}^{\prime}),\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h+L}(x_{h+1:h+L},a_{h:h+L-1};\mathcal{D}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex115"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex115.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\min(D_{\star}(\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h+L}(x_{h+1:h+L},a_{h:h+L-1};\mathcal{D}^{\prime})\|\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h+L}(x_{h+1:h+L},a_{h:h+L-1};\mathcal{D})),1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐛</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mi>𝖺𝗉𝗑</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐛</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mi>𝖺𝗉𝗑</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\min(D_{\star}(\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h+L}(x_{h+1:h+L},a_{h:h+L-1};\mathcal{D}^{\prime})\|\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h+L}(x_{h+1:h+L},a_{h:h+L-1};\mathcal{D})),1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 4^{L}\min(X_{L},1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mn>4</mn><mi>L</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 4^{L}\min(X_{L},1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p12.4" class="ltx_p">since <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(p,q)\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(p,q)\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> for any distributions <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p,q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,q</annotation></semantics></math>.
Fix <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;t\leq L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;t\leq L</annotation></semantics></math> and condition on <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m16" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(x_{h+1:h+t-1},a_{h:h+t-2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{h+1:h+t-1},a_{h:h+t-2})</annotation></semantics></math>, which determines <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. The conditional distribution of <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{h+t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{h+t-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is then <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m19" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi(x_{1:h+t-1},a_{1:h+t-2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(x_{1:h+t-1},a_{1:h+t-2})</annotation></semantics></math>, and for any fixed <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{h+t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{h+t-1}</annotation></semantics></math> the conditional distribution of <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{h+t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{h+t}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m22" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(\mathbb{O}_{h+t})^{\top}\mathbb{P}_{h+t}(a_{h+t-1})\cdot\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h+t-1}(x_{h+1:h+t-1},a_{h:h+t-2};\mathcal{D}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝕆</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐛</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>𝖺𝗉𝗑</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbb{O}_{h+t})^{\top}\mathbb{P}_{h+t}(a_{h+t-1})\cdot\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h+t-1}(x_{h+1:h+t-1},a_{h:h+t-2};\mathcal{D}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> by <a href="#A3.Thmlemma2" title="Lemma C.2. ‣ Appendix C Technical Lemmas ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a> (applied to the modified POMDP that is initialized to a latent state <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{h}\sim\mathcal{D}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{h}\sim\mathcal{D}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> immediately before the action <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> is taken; for this POMDP <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m25" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h+t-1}(x_{h+1:h+t-1},a_{h:h+t-2};\mathcal{D}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐛</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>𝖺𝗉𝗑</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h+t-1}(x_{h+1:h+t-1},a_{h:h+t-2};\mathcal{D}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> is the true belief state). Recall that by definition,</p>
<table id="A4.Ex116" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex116.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h+t}(x_{h+1:h+t},a_{h:h+t-1};\mathcal{D}^{\prime})=\mathbb{U}_{h+t}(\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h+t-1}(x_{h+1:h+t-1},a_{h:h+t-2};\mathcal{D}^{\prime}),a_{h+t-1},x_{h+t})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐛</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>𝖺𝗉𝗑</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝕌</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐛</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>𝖺𝗉𝗑</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h+t}(x_{h+1:h+t},a_{h:h+t-1};\mathcal{D}^{\prime})=\mathbb{U}_{h+t}(\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h+t-1}(x_{h+1:h+t-1},a_{h:h+t-2};\mathcal{D}^{\prime}),a_{h+t-1},x_{h+t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p12.5" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A4.Ex117" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex117.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h+t}(x_{h+1:h+t},a_{h:h+t-1};\mathcal{D})=\mathbb{U}_{h+t}(\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h+t-1}(x_{h+1:h+t-1},a_{h:h+t-2};\mathcal{D}),a_{h+t-1},x_{h+t})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐛</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>𝖺𝗉𝗑</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝕌</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐛</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>𝖺𝗉𝗑</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h+t}(x_{h+1:h+t},a_{h:h+t-1};\mathcal{D})=\mathbb{U}_{h+t}(\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h+t-1}(x_{h+1:h+t-1},a_{h:h+t-2};\mathcal{D}),a_{h+t-1},x_{h+t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p12.6" class="ltx_p">By <a href="#A4.Thmcorollary1" title="Corollary D.1. ‣ D.1 Belief Contraction ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Corollary</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>, it holds in expectation (resp., in probability) over <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{h+t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{h+t}</annotation></semantics></math>, conditioned on the prior history, that</p>
<table id="A4.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex118"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex118.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[X_{t}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[X_{t}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex118.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=4^{-t}\mathbb{E}[D_{\star}(\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h+t}(x_{h+1:h+t},a_{h:h+t-1};\mathcal{D}^{\prime})\|\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h+t}(x_{h+1:h+t},a_{h:h+t-1};\mathcal{D}))]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐛</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>𝖺𝗉𝗑</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐛</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>𝖺𝗉𝗑</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=4^{-t}\mathbb{E}[D_{\star}(\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h+t}(x_{h+1:h+t},a_{h:h+t-1};\mathcal{D}^{\prime})\|\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h+t}(x_{h+1:h+t},a_{h:h+t-1};\mathcal{D}))]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex119"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex119.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 4^{1-t}D_{\star}(\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h+t-1}(x_{h+1:h+t-1},a_{h:h+t-2};\mathcal{D}^{\prime})\|\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h+t-1}(x_{h+1:h+t-1},a_{h:h+t-2};\mathcal{D}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>D</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐛</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>𝖺𝗉𝗑</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐛</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>𝖺𝗉𝗑</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 4^{1-t}D_{\star}(\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h+t-1}(x_{h+1:h+t-1},a_{h:h+t-2};\mathcal{D}^{\prime})\|\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h+t-1}(x_{h+1:h+t-1},a_{h:h+t-2};\mathcal{D}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex120"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex120.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=X_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=X_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p12.7" class="ltx_p">and similarly</p>
<table id="A4.Ex121" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex121.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr[X_{t}&gt;\delta^{1/3}X_{t-1}]\leq 2\delta^{1/3}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr[X_{t}&gt;\delta^{1/3}X_{t-1}]\leq 2\delta^{1/3}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p12.8" class="ltx_p">Since these bounds hold for any fixed <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{h+t-1}\in\mathcal{A}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{h+t-1}\in\mathcal{A}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, they also hold in expectation (resp., in probability) over the joint draws of <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{h+t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{h+t-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{h+t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{h+t}</annotation></semantics></math>, conditioned on any realization of <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m30" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(x_{h+1:h+t-1},a_{h:h+t-2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{h+1:h+t-1},a_{h:h+t-2})</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[X_{t}\mid{}X_{t-1}]\leq X_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[X_{t}\mid{}X_{t-1}]\leq X_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr[X_{t}&gt;\delta^{1/3}X_{t-1}\mid{}X_{t-1}]\leq 2\delta^{1/3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr[X_{t}&gt;\delta^{1/3}X_{t-1}\mid{}X_{t-1}]\leq 2\delta^{1/3}</annotation></semantics></math> both hold almost surely. We can now apply <a href="#A3.Thmlemma5" title="Lemma C.5. ‣ Appendix C Technical Lemmas ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.5</span></a> to the sequence <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X_{0},\dots,X_{L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X_{0},\dots,X_{L})</annotation></semantics></math> with parameters <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S:=\left\lVert\frac{\mathcal{D}^{\prime}}{\mathcal{D}}\right\rVert_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mfrac><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mfrac><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S:=\left\lVert\frac{\mathcal{D}^{\prime}}{\mathcal{D}}\right\rVert_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon:=2\delta^{1/3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon:=2\delta^{1/3}</annotation></semantics></math>; we get that</p>
<table id="A4.Ex122" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex122.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\min(X_{L},1)]\leq\mathbb{E}[\min(X_{L},S)]\leq 2\cdot 3^{L}2^{L/3}\delta^{L/9}\left\lVert\frac{\mathcal{D}^{\prime}}{\mathcal{D}}\right\rVert_{\infty}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mfrac><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mfrac><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\min(X_{L},1)]\leq\mathbb{E}[\min(X_{L},S)]\leq 2\cdot 3^{L}2^{L/3}\delta^{L/9}\left\lVert\frac{\mathcal{D}^{\prime}}{\mathcal{D}}\right\rVert_{\infty}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p12.9" class="ltx_p">Combining this bound with <a href="#A4.E11" title="In D.1 Belief Contraction ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>, and setting <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\ref{thm:belief-contraction}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem D.1. ‣ D.1 Belief Contraction ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a></mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\ref{thm:belief-contraction}}</annotation></semantics></math> to be a sufficiently large constant, completes the proof.
∎
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmremark1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmremark1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark D.1</span></span><span id="A4.Thmremark1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmremark1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmremark1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Any <math id="A4.Thmremark1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>-perturbed Block MDP is <math id="A4.Thmremark1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-observable
with <math id="A4.Thmremark1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=1-2\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=1-2\delta</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#A2.Thmdefinition4" title="Definition B.4 (𝛾-observability ( , )). ‣ B.2 Decodability and 𝛾-Observability ‣ Appendix B Additional Preliminaries ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>): for any <math id="A4.Thmremark1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in[H]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in[H]</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A4.Thmremark1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{O}_{h}=(1-\delta)\widetilde{\mathbb{O}}_{h}+\delta E_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕆</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕆</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{O}_{h}=(1-\delta)\widetilde{\mathbb{O}}_{h}+\delta E_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, and thus given any <math id="A4.Thmremark1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b,b^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b,b^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A4.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex123"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex123.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\lVert\mathbb{O}^{\top}_{h}b-\mathbb{O}^{\top}_{h}b^{\prime}\right\rVert_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝕆</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝕆</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\lVert\mathbb{O}^{\top}_{h}b-\mathbb{O}^{\top}_{h}b^{\prime}\right\rVert_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex123.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left\lVert(1-\delta)\widetilde{\mathbb{O}}^{\top}_{h}(b-b^{\prime})+\delta E_{h}^{\top}(b-b^{\prime})\right\rVert_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕆</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>h</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left\lVert(1-\delta)\widetilde{\mathbb{O}}^{\top}_{h}(b-b^{\prime})+\delta E_{h}^{\top}(b-b^{\prime})\right\rVert_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex124"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex124.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq(1-\delta)\left\lVert\widetilde{\mathbb{O}}^{\top}_{h}(b-b^{\prime})\right\rVert_{1}-\delta\left\lVert E_{h}^{\top}(b-b^{\prime})\right\rVert_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕆</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>h</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq(1-\delta)\left\lVert\widetilde{\mathbb{O}}^{\top}_{h}(b-b^{\prime})\right\rVert_{1}-\delta\left\lVert E_{h}^{\top}(b-b^{\prime})\right\rVert_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex125"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex125.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq(1-\delta)\left\lVert b-b^{\prime}\right\rVert_{1}-\delta\left\lVert E_{h}\right\rVert_{\textrm{op}}\left\lVert b-b^{\prime}\right\rVert_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mtext>op</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq(1-\delta)\left\lVert b-b^{\prime}\right\rVert_{1}-\delta\left\lVert E_{h}\right\rVert_{\textrm{op}}\left\lVert b-b^{\prime}\right\rVert_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex126"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex126.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq(1-2\delta)\left\lVert b-b^{\prime}\right\rVert_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq(1-2\delta)\left\lVert b-b^{\prime}\right\rVert_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmremark1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">because <math id="A4.Thmremark1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathbb{O}}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕆</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathbb{O}}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the block property. It was shown in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Golowich et al., 2023</a>, Theorem 4.7)</cite> that, for any <math id="A4.Thmremark1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-observable POMDP <math id="A4.Thmremark1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math>, the belief contraction error can be bounded as <math id="A4.Thmremark1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{h}^{\mathsf{contract}}(\pi;L)\leq(1-\gamma^{4}/2^{40})^{L}\cdot\mathcal{O}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>𝖼𝗈𝗇𝗍𝗋𝖺𝖼𝗍</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>40</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{h}^{\mathsf{contract}}(\pi;L)\leq(1-\gamma^{4}/2^{40})^{L}\cdot\mathcal{O}(S)</annotation></semantics></math>. However, substituting in <math id="A4.Thmremark1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma:=1-2\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma:=1-2\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, we see that due to the constant factor of <math id="A4.Thmremark1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{40}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>40</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{40}</annotation></semantics></math>, this bound does not asymptotically improve as <math id="A4.Thmremark1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> decreases — indeed, it is never better than <math id="A4.Thmremark1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-1/2^{40})^{L}\cdot\mathcal{O}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>40</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-1/2^{40})^{L}\cdot\mathcal{O}(S)</annotation></semantics></math> — and moreover is vacuous for <math id="A4.Thmremark1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=o(\log S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=o(\log S)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Approximate Decodability</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section we prove <a href="#S4.Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 4.1 (See ). ‣ 4.1 Theoretical Analysis under Deterministic Dynamics ‣ 4 Distillation is Competitive for Deterministic Dynamics ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>, restated below as <a href="#A4.Thmproposition1" title="Proposition D.1. ‣ D.2 Approximate Decodability ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>, which states that for <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>-perturbed Block MDPs with <em id="A4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">deterministic</em> latent transitions, the decodability error decays exponentially. The proof is somewhat analogous to that of <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem D.1. ‣ D.1 Belief Contraction ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>; the key difference is that the claim that the transitions do not increase decodability error is only true for deterministic transitions (whereas the analogous claim for belief contraction error is unconditionally true).</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For notational convenience, we make the following definition of the “<math id="A4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> variance” <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(b)</annotation></semantics></math> for a given distribution <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmdefinition4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmdefinition4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition D.4</span></span><span id="A4.Thmdefinition4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmdefinition4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmdefinition4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmdefinition4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any set <math id="A4.Thmdefinition4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> and distribution <math id="A4.Thmdefinition4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\in\Delta(\mathcal{S})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\in\Delta(\mathcal{S})</annotation></semantics></math>, define <math id="A4.Thmdefinition4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(b):=1-\left\lVert b\right\rVert_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(b):=1-\left\lVert b\right\rVert_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The following lemma shows that the <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> variance contracts by <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{poly}(\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>poly</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{poly}(\delta)</annotation></semantics></math> with high probability under the Bayes operator.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmlemma3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmlemma3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.3</span></span><span id="A4.Thmlemma3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmlemma3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.Thmlemma3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmlemma3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A4.Thmlemma3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and suppose that <math id="A4.Thmlemma3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="A4.Thmlemma3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>-perturbed Block MDP with deterministic latent transitions (but potentially stochastic initial state). Fix <math id="A4.Thmlemma3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in[H]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in[H]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmlemma3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\in\Delta(\mathcal{S}_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\in\Delta(\mathcal{S}_{h})</annotation></semantics></math>. Draw <math id="A4.Thmlemma3.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x\sim\mathbb{O}_{h}(\cdot\mid{}b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>𝕆</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\sim\mathbb{O}_{h}(\cdot\mid{}b)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A4.Thmlemma3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{B}_{h}(b;x))]\leq\min(\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(b),\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{B}_{h}(b;x))]\leq\min(\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(b),\delta)</annotation></semantics></math> and</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex127" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex127.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr[\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{B}_{h}(b;x))&gt;\delta^{1/3}\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(b)]\leq 3\delta^{1/3}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr[\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{B}_{h}(b;x))&gt;\delta^{1/3}\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(b)]\leq 3\delta^{1/3}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof. </span>Pick any <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{\star}\in\mathcal{S}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\star}\in\mathcal{S}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{s^{\star}}=\left\lVert b\right\rVert_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{s^{\star}}=\left\lVert b\right\rVert_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>, and hence <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{s\in\mathcal{S}_{h}\setminus\{s^{\star}\}}b(s)=\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{s\in\mathcal{S}_{h}\setminus\{s^{\star}\}}b(s)=\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(b)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</p>
<table id="A4.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex128"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex128.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{B}_{h}(b;x))]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{B}_{h}(b;x))]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex128.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{h}}\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}b)\left(1-\max_{s\in\mathcal{S}_{h}}\mathbb{B}_{h}(b;x)(s)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝕆</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{h}}\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}b)\left(1-\max_{s\in\mathcal{S}_{h}}\mathbb{B}_{h}(b;x)(s)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex129"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex129.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{h}}\min_{s\in\mathcal{S}_{h}}\left(\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}b)-b(s)\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}s)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝕆</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕆</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{h}}\min_{s\in\mathcal{S}_{h}}\left(\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}b)-b(s)\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}s)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{h}}\min_{s\in\mathcal{S}_{h}}\sum_{s^{\prime}\in\mathcal{S}_{h}\setminus\{s\}}b(s^{\prime})\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}s^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mmultiscripts><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts></mstyle><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕆</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{h}}\min_{s\in\mathcal{S}_{h}}\sum_{s^{\prime}\in\mathcal{S}_{h}\setminus\{s\}}b(s^{\prime})\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}s^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where the second equality is by the definition <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{B}_{h}(b;x)(s):=\frac{b(s)\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}s)}{\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}b)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕆</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝕆</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{B}_{h}(b;x)(s):=\frac{b(s)\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}s)}{\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}b)}</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#A2.Thmdefinition1" title="Definition B.1 (Belief state update ( , )). ‣ B.1 Belief states ‣ Appendix B Additional Preliminaries ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>). First, <a href="#A4.E12" title="In D.2 Approximate Decodability ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> implies that</p>
<table id="A4.Ex130" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex130.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{B}_{h}(b;x))]\leq\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{h}}\sum_{s^{\prime}\in\mathcal{S}_{h}\setminus\{s^{\star}\}}b(s^{\prime})\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}s^{\prime})=\sum_{s^{\prime}\in\mathcal{S}_{h}\setminus\{s^{\star}\}}b(s^{\prime})=\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(b)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕆</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{B}_{h}(b;x))]\leq\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{h}}\sum_{s^{\prime}\in\mathcal{S}_{h}\setminus\{s^{\star}\}}b(s^{\prime})\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}s^{\prime})=\sum_{s^{\prime}\in\mathcal{S}_{h}\setminus\{s^{\star}\}}b(s^{\prime})=\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(b),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p">where the first equality uses the fact that <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{O}_{h}(\cdot\mid{}s^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕆</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{O}_{h}(\cdot\mid{}s^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> is a distribution for any fixed <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Next, <a href="#A4.E12" title="In D.2 Approximate Decodability ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> implies that</p>
<table id="A4.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex131"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex131.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{B}_{h}(b;x))]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{B}_{h}(b;x))]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex131.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{h}}\sum_{s^{\prime}\in\mathcal{S}_{h}\setminus\{\phi(x)\}}b(s^{\prime})\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}s^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕆</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{h}}\sum_{s^{\prime}\in\mathcal{S}_{h}\setminus\{\phi(x)\}}b(s^{\prime})\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}s^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex132"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex132.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\delta\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{h}}\sum_{s^{\prime}\in\mathcal{S}_{h}\setminus\{\phi(x)\}}b(s^{\prime})E_{h}(x\mid{}s^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\delta\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{h}}\sum_{s^{\prime}\in\mathcal{S}_{h}\setminus\{\phi(x)\}}b(s^{\prime})E_{h}(x\mid{}s^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex133"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex133.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\delta\sum_{s^{\prime}\in\mathcal{S}_{h}}b(s^{\prime})\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{h}:\phi(x)\neq s^{\prime}}E_{h}(x\mid{}s^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>δ</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\delta\sum_{s^{\prime}\in\mathcal{S}_{h}}b(s^{\prime})\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{h}:\phi(x)\neq s^{\prime}}E_{h}(x\mid{}s^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex134"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex134.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\delta\sum_{s^{\prime}\in\mathcal{S}_{h}}b(s^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\delta\sum_{s^{\prime}\in\mathcal{S}_{h}}b(s^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\delta." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p4.4" class="ltx_p">This, together with the preceding bound, proves the first claim of the lemma. Now consider the event that <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(x)=s^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(x)=s^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}b)\geq(1-\delta)b(\phi(x))\widetilde{\mathbb{O}}_{h}(x\mid{}\phi(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝕆</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕆</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}b)\geq(1-\delta)b(\phi(x))\widetilde{\mathbb{O}}_{h}(x\mid{}\phi(x))</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A4.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr[\phi(x)\neq s^{\star}]=1-\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{h}:\phi(x)=s^{\star}}\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}b)\leq 1-(1-\delta)b(s^{\star})=1-(1-\delta)(1-\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(b))\leq\delta+\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(b).\addcontentsline{lla}{section}{\hbox to20.74pt{\crtrefnumber{eq:vinf-bad-event}\hfil}eq:vinf-bad-event}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mi>𝕆</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr[\phi(x)\neq s^{\star}]=1-\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{h}:\phi(x)=s^{\star}}\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}b)\leq 1-(1-\delta)b(s^{\star})=1-(1-\delta)(1-\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(b))\leq\delta+\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(b).\addcontentsline{lla}{section}{\hbox to20.74pt{\crtrefnumber{eq:vinf-bad-event}\hfil}eq:vinf-bad-event}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p4.5" class="ltx_p">Moreover, by an analogous calculation as <a href="#A4.E12" title="In D.2 Approximate Decodability ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>,</p>
<table id="A4.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex135"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex135.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{B}_{h}(b;x))\mathbbm{1}[\phi(x)=s^{\star}]]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{B}_{h}(b;x))\mathbbm{1}[\phi(x)=s^{\star}]]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex135.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{h}:\phi(x)=s^{\star}}\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}b)\left(1-\max_{s\in\mathcal{S}_{h}}\mathbb{B}_{h}(b;x)(s)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>𝕆</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></munder><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{h}:\phi(x)=s^{\star}}\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}b)\left(1-\max_{s\in\mathcal{S}_{h}}\mathbb{B}_{h}(b;x)(s)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex136"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex136.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{h}:\phi(x)=s^{\star}}\min_{s\in\mathcal{S}_{h}}\left(\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}b)-b(s)\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}s)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝕆</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝕆</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{h}:\phi(x)=s^{\star}}\min_{s\in\mathcal{S}_{h}}\left(\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}b)-b(s)\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}s)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex137"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex137.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{h}:\phi(x)=s^{\star}}\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}b)-b(s^{\star})\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}s^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>𝕆</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝕆</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{h}:\phi(x)=s^{\star}}\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}b)-b(s^{\star})\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}s^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex138"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex138.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{h}:\phi(x)=s^{\star}}\sum_{s\in\mathcal{S}_{h}\setminus\{s^{\star}\}}b(s)\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝕆</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{h}:\phi(x)=s^{\star}}\sum_{s\in\mathcal{S}_{h}\setminus\{s^{\star}\}}b(s)\mathbb{O}_{h}(x\mid{}s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex139"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex139.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\delta\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{h}:\phi(x)=s^{\star}}\sum_{s\in\mathcal{S}_{h}\setminus\{s^{\star}\}}b(s)E_{h}(x\mid{}s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>δ</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\delta\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{h}:\phi(x)=s^{\star}}\sum_{s\in\mathcal{S}_{h}\setminus\{s^{\star}\}}b(s)E_{h}(x\mid{}s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex140"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex140.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\delta\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(b)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\delta\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(b).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p4.6" class="ltx_p">It follows that</p>
<table id="A4.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex141"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex141.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr[\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{B}_{h}(b;x))&gt;\delta^{1/3}\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(b)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr[\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{B}_{h}(b;x))&gt;\delta^{1/3}\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(b)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex141.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\Pr[\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{B}_{h}(b;x))\mathbbm{1}[\phi(x)=s^{\star}]&gt;\delta^{1/3}\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(b)]+\Pr[\phi(x)\neq s^{\star}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\Pr[\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{B}_{h}(b;x))\mathbbm{1}[\phi(x)=s^{\star}]&gt;\delta^{1/3}\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(b)]+\Pr[\phi(x)\neq s^{\star}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex142"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex142.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\delta^{2/3}+\delta+\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\delta^{2/3}+\delta+\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(b)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p4.7" class="ltx_p">by Markov’s inequality and <a href="#A4.E14" title="In D.2 Approximate Decodability ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>. To conclude, we distinguish two cases. If <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(b)\leq\delta^{1/3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(b)\leq\delta^{1/3}</annotation></semantics></math>, then we get</p>
<table id="A4.Ex143" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex143.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr[\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{B}_{h}(b;x))&gt;\delta^{1/3}\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(b)]\leq\delta^{2/3}+\delta+\delta^{1/3}\leq 3\delta^{1/3}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr[\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{B}_{h}(b;x))&gt;\delta^{1/3}\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(b)]\leq\delta^{2/3}+\delta+\delta^{1/3}\leq 3\delta^{1/3}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p4.8" class="ltx_p">as needed. Otherwise, <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(b)&gt;\delta^{1/3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(b)&gt;\delta^{1/3}</annotation></semantics></math>, so</p>
<table id="A4.Ex144" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex144.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr[\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{B}_{h}(b;x))&gt;\delta^{1/3}\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(b)]\leq\Pr[\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{B}_{h}(b;x))&gt;\delta^{2/3}]\leq\delta^{1/3}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr[\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{B}_{h}(b;x))&gt;\delta^{1/3}\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(b)]\leq\Pr[\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{B}_{h}(b;x))&gt;\delta^{2/3}]\leq\delta^{1/3}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p4.9" class="ltx_p">by Markov’s inequality and <a href="#A4.E13" title="In D.2 Approximate Decodability ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>. This completes the proof.
∎
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Using <a href="#A4.Thmlemma3" title="Lemma D.3. ‣ D.2 Approximate Decodability ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a> and the assumption of deterministic latent dynamics, it is straightforward to show that the <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> variance contracts by <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{poly}(\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>poly</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{poly}(\delta)</annotation></semantics></math> with high probability under the <em id="A4.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">belief update</em> operator:</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmcorollary2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmcorollary2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary D.2</span></span><span id="A4.Thmcorollary2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmcorollary2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.Thmcorollary2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A4.Thmcorollary2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and suppose that <math id="A4.Thmcorollary2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="A4.Thmcorollary2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>-perturbed Block MDP with deterministic latent transitions (but potentially stochastic initial state). Fix <math id="A4.Thmcorollary2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in[H]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in[H]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmcorollary2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\in\Delta(\mathcal{S}_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\in\Delta(\mathcal{S}_{h})</annotation></semantics></math>. For any action <math id="A4.Thmcorollary2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{h-1}\in\mathcal{A}_{h-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{h-1}\in\mathcal{A}_{h-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, with expectation over <math id="A4.Thmcorollary2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{h}\sim(\mathbb{O}_{h})^{\top}\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})\cdot b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝕆</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{h}\sim(\mathbb{O}_{h})^{\top}\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})\cdot b</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that <math id="A4.Thmcorollary2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{U}_{h}(b;a_{h-1},x_{h}))]\leq\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕌</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{U}_{h}(b;a_{h-1},x_{h}))]\leq\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(b)</annotation></semantics></math> and</p>
<table id="A4.Ex145" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex145.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr[\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{U}_{h}(b;a_{h-1},x_{h}))&gt;\delta^{1/3}\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(b)]\leq 3\delta^{1/3}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝕌</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr[\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{U}_{h}(b;a_{h-1},x_{h}))&gt;\delta^{1/3}\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(b)]\leq 3\delta^{1/3}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof. </span>From <a href="#A2.Thmdefinition1" title="Definition B.1 (Belief state update ( , )). ‣ B.1 Belief states ‣ Appendix B Additional Preliminaries ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, we have for any <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> that <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{U}_{h}(b;a_{h-1},x_{h})=\mathbb{B}_{h}(\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})\cdot b;x_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝕌</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{U}_{h}(b;a_{h-1},x_{h})=\mathbb{B}_{h}(\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})\cdot b;x_{h})</annotation></semantics></math>. Applying <a href="#A4.Thmlemma3" title="Lemma D.3. ‣ D.2 Approximate Decodability ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a> to the distribution <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})\cdot b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})\cdot b</annotation></semantics></math> (observe that <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> is indeed distributed according to <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{O}_{h}(\cdot\mid{}\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})\cdot b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕆</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{O}_{h}(\cdot\mid{}\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})\cdot b)</annotation></semantics></math>), we get <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{U}_{h}(b;a_{h-1},x_{h}))]\leq\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})\cdot b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕌</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{U}_{h}(b;a_{h-1},x_{h}))]\leq\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})\cdot b)</annotation></semantics></math> and</p>
<table id="A4.Ex146" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex146.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr[\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{U}_{h}(b;a_{h-1},x_{h}))&gt;\delta^{1/3}\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})\cdot b)]\leq 3\delta^{1/3}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝕌</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr[\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{U}_{h}(b;a_{h-1},x_{h}))&gt;\delta^{1/3}\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})\cdot b)]\leq 3\delta^{1/3}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p">To complete the proof, it suffices to show that <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})\cdot b)\leq\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})\cdot b)\leq\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(b)</annotation></semantics></math>. Indeed, since the transitions are deterministic, the matrix <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})\in\mathbb{R}^{|\mathcal{S}_{h}|\times|\mathcal{S}_{h-1}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})\in\mathbb{R}^{|\mathcal{S}_{h}|\times|\mathcal{S}_{h-1}|}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies that every column is a standard basis vector. Identify any <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{\star}\in\mathcal{S}_{h-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\star}\in\mathcal{S}_{h-1}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{s^{\star}}=\left\lVert b\right\rVert_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{s^{\star}}=\left\lVert b\right\rVert_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then there is some <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{h}\in\mathcal{S}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{h}\in\mathcal{S}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})_{s_{h},s^{\star}}=\mathbb{P}_{h}(s_{h}\mid{}s^{\star},a_{h-1})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})_{s_{h},s^{\star}}=\mathbb{P}_{h}(s_{h}\mid{}s^{\star},a_{h-1})=1</annotation></semantics></math>. But then the entry of <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})\cdot b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})\cdot b</annotation></semantics></math> indexed by <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> is at least <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{s^{\star}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{s^{\star}}</annotation></semantics></math>. So indeed <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})\cdot b)\leq\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{P}_{h}(a_{h-1})\cdot b)\leq\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(b)</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">We can now prove the following restatement of <a href="#S4.Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 4.1 (See ). ‣ 4.1 Theoretical Analysis under Deterministic Dynamics ‣ 4 Distillation is Competitive for Deterministic Dynamics ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmproposition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmproposition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition D.1</span></span><span id="A4.Thmproposition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmproposition1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.Thmproposition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmproposition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There is a universal constant <math id="A4.Thmproposition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\ref{prop:vinf-decay}}&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#A4.Thmproposition1" title="Proposition D.1. ‣ D.2 Approximate Decodability ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a></mtext></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\ref{prop:vinf-decay}}&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> so that the following holds. Let <math id="A4.Thmproposition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and suppose that <math id="A4.Thmproposition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="A4.Thmproposition1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>-perturbed Block MDP with deterministic latent transitions (but potentially stochastic initial state). Fix any executable policy <math id="A4.Thmproposition1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> and index <math id="A4.Thmproposition1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in[H]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in[H]</annotation></semantics></math>. It holds that</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex147" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex147.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}^{\pi}[\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1}))]\leq\min(\delta,(C_{\ref{prop:vinf-decay}}\delta)^{(h-1)/9})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#A4.Thmproposition1" title="Proposition D.1. ‣ D.2 Approximate Decodability ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a></mtext></msub><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}^{\pi}[\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1}))]\leq\min(\delta,(C_{\ref{prop:vinf-decay}}\delta)^{(h-1)/9}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof. </span>Define a sequence of random variables <math id="A4.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="X_{t}:=\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbf{b}_{t}(x_{1:t},a_{1:t-1}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}:=\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbf{b}_{t}(x_{1:t},a_{1:t-1}))</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A4.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq t\leq h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq t\leq h</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A4.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})</annotation></semantics></math> is a random trajectory drawn from policy <math id="A4.SS2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>. We have <math id="A4.SS2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> almost surely. By the same argument as in <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem D.1. ‣ D.1 Belief Contraction ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a> (except using <a href="#A4.Thmcorollary2" title="Corollary D.2. ‣ D.2 Approximate Decodability ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Corollary</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a> rather than <a href="#A4.Thmcorollary1" title="Corollary D.1. ‣ D.1 Belief Contraction ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Corollary</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>), we have for all <math id="A4.SS2.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1&lt;t\leq h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1&lt;t\leq h</annotation></semantics></math> that <math id="A4.SS2.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[X_{t}\mid{}X_{t-1}]\leq X_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[X_{t}\mid{}X_{t-1}]\leq X_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr[X_{t}&gt;\delta^{1/3}X_{t-1}\mid{}X_{t-1}]\leq 3\delta^{1/3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr[X_{t}&gt;\delta^{1/3}X_{t-1}\mid{}X_{t-1}]\leq 3\delta^{1/3}</annotation></semantics></math> hold almost surely. Thus, <a href="#A3.Thmlemma5" title="Lemma C.5. ‣ Appendix C Technical Lemmas ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.5</span></a> applied to <math id="A4.SS2.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X_{1},\dots,X_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X_{1},\dots,X_{h})</annotation></semantics></math> with parameters <math id="A4.SS2.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S:=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>:=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S:=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon:=3\delta^{1/3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon:=3\delta^{1/3}</annotation></semantics></math> implies that</p>
<table id="A4.Ex148" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex148.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[X_{h}]=\mathbb{E}[\min(X_{h},1)]\leq 2\cdot 3^{h-1}3^{(h-1)/3}\delta^{(h-1)/9}\leq(C_{\ref{prop:vinf-decay}}\delta)^{(h-1)/9}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#A4.Thmproposition1" title="Proposition D.1. ‣ D.2 Approximate Decodability ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a></mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[X_{h}]=\mathbb{E}[\min(X_{h},1)]\leq 2\cdot 3^{h-1}3^{(h-1)/3}\delta^{(h-1)/9}\leq(C_{\ref{prop:vinf-decay}}\delta)^{(h-1)/9}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p8.2" class="ltx_p">so long as <math id="A4.SS2.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\ref{prop:vinf-decay}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#A4.Thmproposition1" title="Proposition D.1. ‣ D.2 Approximate Decodability ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a></mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\ref{prop:vinf-decay}}</annotation></semantics></math> is sufficiently large. Additionally, we know that <math id="A4.SS2.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{b}_{1}(x_{1})=\mathbb{B}_{1}(\mathbb{P}_{1};x_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{b}_{1}(x_{1})=\mathbb{B}_{1}(\mathbb{P}_{1};x_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> so</p>
<table id="A4.Ex149" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex149.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[X_{1}]=\mathbb{E}^{\pi}[\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{B}_{1}(\mathbb{P}_{1};x_{1}))]\leq\delta" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[X_{1}]=\mathbb{E}^{\pi}[\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{B}_{1}(\mathbb{P}_{1};x_{1}))]\leq\delta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p8.3" class="ltx_p">by <a href="#A4.Thmlemma3" title="Lemma D.3. ‣ D.2 Approximate Decodability ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a> and the fact that <math id="A4.SS2.p8.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> has distribution <math id="A4.SS2.p8.m15" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{O}_{1}(\cdot\mid{}\mathbb{P}_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕆</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{O}_{1}(\cdot\mid{}\mathbb{P}_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, <math id="A4.SS2.p8.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[X_{t}]\leq\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[X_{t}]\leq\delta</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A4.SS2.p8.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq t\leq h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq t\leq h</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Misspecification Lower Bound for Stochastic Dynamics</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section we prove the following restatement of <a href="#S5.Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 5.1 (See ). ‣ 5.1 Theoretical Analysis under Stochastic Dynamics ‣ 5 RL Outperforms Distillation for Stochastic Dynamics ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>, which shows that in a <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>-perturbed Block MDP with general (stochastic) latent transitions, the misspecification of the optimal latent policy with respect to the class of executable policies can be as large as <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega(\delta H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega(\delta H)</annotation></semantics></math> (for <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\leq 1/H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\leq 1/H</annotation></semantics></math>). This implies an analogous lower bound on decodability error, i.e. it cannot improve exponentially as <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> increases, unlike the case of deterministic latent transitions. Moreover, it shows a fundamental source of (horizon-dependent) error that is not mitigated by increasing the frame-stack <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>: since the following bound applies to all executable policies, it also applies to the class of <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-step executable policies for any <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmproposition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmproposition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition D.2</span></span><span id="A4.Thmproposition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmproposition2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.Thmproposition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmproposition2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A4.Thmproposition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmproposition2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>. There is a <math id="A4.Thmproposition2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>-perturbed Block MDP <math id="A4.Thmproposition2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math> with horizon <math id="A4.Thmproposition2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> such that the optimal latent policy <math id="A4.Thmproposition2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex150" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex150.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{\pi\in\Pi}\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{P}^{\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}},\mathbb{P}^{\pi})\geq\Omega(\min(1,\delta H))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{\pi\in\Pi}\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{P}^{\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}},\mathbb{P}^{\pi})\geq\Omega(\min(1,\delta H))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmproposition2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmproposition2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A4.Thmproposition2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi</annotation></semantics></math> is the class of executable policies.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof. </span>We define <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows. For all <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in[H]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in[H]</annotation></semantics></math>, define the latent state space and observation space to be <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{h}:=\mathcal{X}_{h}:=\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{h}:=\mathcal{X}_{h}:=\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>; also define <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{h}:=\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{h}:=\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let the initial distribution and latent transition dynamics at each step be uniformly random (independent of the previous state and action). For each <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in[H]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in[H]</annotation></semantics></math>, define the reward function <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{h}:\mathcal{S}_{h}\times\mathcal{A}_{h}\to[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{h}:\mathcal{S}_{h}\times\mathcal{A}_{h}\to[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> be defined by <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R_{h}(s,a)=\frac{1}{H}\mathbbm{1}[s=a]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>H</mi></mfrac><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{h}(s,a)=\frac{1}{H}\mathbbm{1}[s=a]</annotation></semantics></math>. Define the observation distribution <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{O}_{h}:\mathcal{S}_{h}\to\Delta(\mathcal{S}_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕆</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{O}_{h}:\mathcal{S}_{h}\to\Delta(\mathcal{S}_{h})</annotation></semantics></math> so that <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{O}_{h}(s\mid{}s)=1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝕆</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{O}_{h}(s\mid{}s)=1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{O}_{h}(1-s\mid{}s)=\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝕆</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{O}_{h}(1-s\mid{}s)=\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">It is clear that <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>-perturbed Block MDP. Under the trajectory distribution <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}}</annotation></semantics></math> induced by the optimal latent policy <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{h}=s_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{h}=s_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in[H]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in[H]</annotation></semantics></math> with probability <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>. However, for any executable policy <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>, for any step <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> and history <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tau_{1:h-1}=(s_{1:h-1},x_{1:h-1},a_{1:h-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{1:h-1}=(s_{1:h-1},x_{1:h-1},a_{1:h-1})</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr^{\pi}[a_{h}=s_{h}\mid{}\tau_{1:h-1}]\leq 1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Pr</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr^{\pi}[a_{h}=s_{h}\mid{}\tau_{1:h-1}]\leq 1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math> since the prior history is independent of <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the conditional distribution <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{h}\mid{}x_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{h}\mid{}x_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> has only <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math> mass on <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus,</p>
<table id="A4.Ex151" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex151.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr^{\pi}[\forall h\in[H]:a_{h}=s_{h}]\leq(1-\delta)^{H}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Pr</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>H</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr^{\pi}[\forall h\in[H]:a_{h}=s_{h}]\leq(1-\delta)^{H}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\geq 1/H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\geq 1/H</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\delta)^{H}\leq e^{-1}\leq 1-\Omega(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>H</mi></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\delta)^{H}\leq e^{-1}\leq 1-\Omega(1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Otherwise, <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\delta)^{H}\leq 1-\Omega(\delta H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>H</mi></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\delta)^{H}\leq 1-\Omega(\delta H)</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{P}^{\pi},\mathbb{P}^{\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}})\geq\Omega(\min(1,\delta H))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{P}^{\pi},\mathbb{P}^{\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}})\geq\Omega(\min(1,\delta H))</annotation></semantics></math> as claimed.
∎
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Omitted Proofs for Expert Distillation</h2>

<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Misspecification Bounds for Composed Policies</h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section we prove upper bounds on the misspecification of a latent policy (with respect to certain executable policies obtained by <em id="A5.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">composing</em> the latent with some belief state) in terms of instance-dependent error metrics. The first main result is <a href="#A5.Thmlemma3" title="Lemma E.3. ‣ E.1 Misspecification Bounds for Composed Policies ‣ Appendix E Omitted Proofs for Expert Distillation ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.3</span></a> (a restatement of <a href="#S3.Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 3.1 (See ). ‣ 3.2 Errors in POMDPs ‣ 3 Approximate Decodability and Belief Contraction ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>), where the upper bound is in terms of decodability error (<a href="#S3.Thmdefinition1" title="Definition 3.1 (Decodability Error). ‣ 3.2 Errors in POMDPs ‣ 3 Approximate Decodability and Belief Contraction ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>) and error in approximating the true belief state. The second main result is <a href="#A5.Thmlemma4" title="Lemma E.4. ‣ E.1 Misspecification Bounds for Composed Policies ‣ Appendix E Omitted Proofs for Expert Distillation ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.4</span></a>, where the decodability error term is replaced by <em id="A5.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">action-prediction error</em> (<a href="#S6.Thmdefinition1" title="Definition 6.1 (Action-prediction error). ‣ Smoothness of the latent policy ‣ 6 Towards Better Distillation: Imitating a Smoother Expert ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To prove <a href="#A5.Thmlemma3" title="Lemma E.3. ‣ E.1 Misspecification Bounds for Composed Policies ‣ Appendix E Omitted Proofs for Expert Distillation ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.3</span></a>, it is convenient to first analyze the policy that samples a state from the true belief state induced by the current history, and then samples an action from <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}</annotation></semantics></math> accordingly. The key technical observation, below, encapsulates the intuition that resampling a near-deterministic random variable is likely to yield the same realization.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma E.1</span></span><span id="A5.Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A5.Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{Y,Y_{\mathsf{nuis}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>𝗇𝗎𝗂𝗌</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{Y,Y_{\mathsf{nuis}}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a joint distribution over random variables <math id="A5.Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Y,Y_{\mathsf{nuis}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>𝗇𝗎𝗂𝗌</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Y,Y_{\mathsf{nuis}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A5.Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{Z|Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{Z|Y}</annotation></semantics></math> be a conditional distribution. Define <math id="A5.Thmlemma1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Q}_{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℚ</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Q}_{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows. Resample <math id="A5.Thmlemma1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y^{\prime}\sim\mathbb{P}_{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y^{\prime}\sim\mathbb{P}_{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> and then sample <math id="A5.Thmlemma1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\sim\mathbb{P}_{Z|Y^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\sim\mathbb{P}_{Z|Y^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex152" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex152.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{P}_{Y,Y_{\mathsf{nuis}}}\mathbb{P}_{Z|Y},\mathbb{P}_{Y,Y_{\mathsf{nuis}}}\mathbb{Q}_{Z})\leq 2\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{P}_{Y})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>𝗇𝗎𝗂𝗌</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>𝗇𝗎𝗂𝗌</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ℚ</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{P}_{Y,Y_{\mathsf{nuis}}}\mathbb{P}_{Z|Y},\mathbb{P}_{Y,Y_{\mathsf{nuis}}}\mathbb{Q}_{Z})\leq 2\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{P}_{Y}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmlemma1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmlemma1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Additionally,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex153" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex153.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{P}_{Y,Y_{\mathsf{nuis}}}\mathbb{P}_{Z|Y},\mathbb{P}_{Y,Y_{\mathsf{nuis}}}\mathbb{Q}_{Z})\leq 2\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{P}_{Z})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>𝗇𝗎𝗂𝗌</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>𝗇𝗎𝗂𝗌</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ℚ</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{P}_{Y,Y_{\mathsf{nuis}}}\mathbb{P}_{Z|Y},\mathbb{P}_{Y,Y_{\mathsf{nuis}}}\mathbb{Q}_{Z})\leq 2\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{P}_{Z}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof. </span>Consider the process where we draw <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Y,Y_{\mathsf{nuis}})\sim\mathbb{P}_{Y,Y_{\mathsf{nuis}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>𝗇𝗎𝗂𝗌</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>𝗇𝗎𝗂𝗌</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Y,Y_{\mathsf{nuis}})\sim\mathbb{P}_{Y,Y_{\mathsf{nuis}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\sim\mathbb{P}_{Z|Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\sim\mathbb{P}_{Z|Y}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y^{\prime}\sim\mathbb{P}_{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y^{\prime}\sim\mathbb{P}_{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y^{\prime}=Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y^{\prime}=Y</annotation></semantics></math> then we set <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{\prime}=Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{\prime}=Z</annotation></semantics></math>; otherwise we sample <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{\prime}\sim\mathbb{P}_{Z|Y^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{\prime}\sim\mathbb{P}_{Z|Y^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Y,Y_{\mathsf{nuis}},Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>𝗇𝗎𝗂𝗌</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Y,Y_{\mathsf{nuis}},Z)</annotation></semantics></math> is distributed according to <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{Y,Y_{\mathsf{nuis}}}\mathbb{P}_{Z|Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>𝗇𝗎𝗂𝗌</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{Y,Y_{\mathsf{nuis}}}\mathbb{P}_{Z|Y}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Y,Y_{\mathsf{nuis}},Z^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>𝗇𝗎𝗂𝗌</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Y,Y_{\mathsf{nuis}},Z^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> is distributed according to <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{Y,Y_{\mathsf{nuis}}}\mathbb{Q}_{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>𝗇𝗎𝗂𝗌</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ℚ</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{Y,Y_{\mathsf{nuis}}}\mathbb{Q}_{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, we have defined a coupling. Moreover,</p>
<table id="A5.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex154"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex154.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr[(Y,Y_{\mathsf{nuis}},Z)\neq(Y,Y_{\mathsf{nuis}},Z^{\prime})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>𝗇𝗎𝗂𝗌</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>𝗇𝗎𝗂𝗌</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr[(Y,Y_{\mathsf{nuis}},Z)\neq(Y,Y_{\mathsf{nuis}},Z^{\prime})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex154.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\Pr[Y\neq Y^{\prime}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\Pr[Y\neq Y^{\prime}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex155"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex155.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\Pr[Y\neq\argmax_{y}\mathbb{P}_{Y}(y)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>≠</mo><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mi>y</mi></msub><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\Pr[Y\neq\argmax_{y}\mathbb{P}_{Y}(y)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex156"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex156.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{P}_{Y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{P}_{Y})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">as needed for the first claim. For the second claim,</p>
<table id="A5.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex157"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex157.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr[(Y,Y_{\mathsf{nuis}},Z)\neq(Y,Y_{\mathsf{nuis}},Z^{\prime})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>𝗇𝗎𝗂𝗌</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>𝗇𝗎𝗂𝗌</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr[(Y,Y_{\mathsf{nuis}},Z)\neq(Y,Y_{\mathsf{nuis}},Z^{\prime})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex157.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\Pr[Z\neq Z^{\prime}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\Pr[Z\neq Z^{\prime}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex158"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex158.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{P}_{Z})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbb{P}_{Z})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">as needed.
∎
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma E.2</span></span><span id="A5.Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A5.Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}\in\Pi^{\mathsf{latent}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}\in\Pi^{\mathsf{latent}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a latent (Markovian) policy and define the executable policy <math id="A5.Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex159" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex159.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1}):=\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}\circ\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1}):=\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}\circ\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmlemma2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmlemma2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex160" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex160.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{P}^{\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}},\mathbb{P}^{\pi})\leq 2\sum_{h=1}^{H}\mathbb{E}^{\pi}[\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1}))]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{P}^{\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}},\mathbb{P}^{\pi})\leq 2\sum_{h=1}^{H}\mathbb{E}^{\pi}[\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1}))].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof. </span>For each <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq h\leq H+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq h\leq H+1</annotation></semantics></math> let <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\circ_{h}\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>h</mi></msub><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\circ_{h}\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the policy that follows <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> for the first <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h-1</annotation></semantics></math> actions and subsequently follows <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\circ_{1}\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}=\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\circ_{1}\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}=\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\circ_{H+1}\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}=\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\circ_{H+1}\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}=\pi</annotation></semantics></math>, it suffices to show that, for each <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in[H]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in[H]</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A5.Ex161" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex161.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{P}^{\pi\circ_{h}\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}},\mathbb{P}^{\pi\circ_{h+1}\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}})\leq 2\mathbb{E}^{\pi}[\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1}))]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>h</mi></msub><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{P}^{\pi\circ_{h}\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}},\mathbb{P}^{\pi\circ_{h+1}\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}})\leq 2\mathbb{E}^{\pi}[\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1}))].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Observe that both distributions have the same conditional distributions over <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(s_{h+1:H},x_{h+1:H},a_{h+1:H})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s_{h+1:H},x_{h+1:H},a_{h+1:H})</annotation></semantics></math> given <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(s_{1:h},x_{1:h},a_{1:h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s_{1:h},x_{1:h},a_{1:h})</annotation></semantics></math>. By this fact and the data processing inequality,</p>
<table id="A5.Ex162" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex162.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{P}^{\pi\circ_{h}\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}},\mathbb{P}^{\pi\circ_{h+1}\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}})=\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{P}^{\pi\circ_{h}\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}}_{X,Y,Y_{\mathsf{nuis}},Z},\mathbb{P}^{\pi\circ_{h+1}\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}}_{X,Y,Y_{\mathsf{nuis}},Z})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>h</mi></msub><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>𝗇𝗎𝗂𝗌</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>h</mi></msub><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>𝗇𝗎𝗂𝗌</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{P}^{\pi\circ_{h}\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}},\mathbb{P}^{\pi\circ_{h+1}\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}})=\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{P}^{\pi\circ_{h}\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}}_{X,Y,Y_{\mathsf{nuis}},Z},\mathbb{P}^{\pi\circ_{h+1}\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}}_{X,Y,Y_{\mathsf{nuis}},Z})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="X=(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=s_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=s_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Y_{\mathsf{nuis}}=s_{1:h-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝗇𝗎𝗂𝗌</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{\mathsf{nuis}}=s_{1:h-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=a_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=a_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>. Both distributions have the same marginal over <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X,Y,Y_{\mathsf{nuis}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>𝗇𝗎𝗂𝗌</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X,Y,Y_{\mathsf{nuis}})</annotation></semantics></math>. The distribution of <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y|X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y|X</annotation></semantics></math> is precisely <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m17" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})</annotation></semantics></math> by <a href="#A3.Thmlemma2" title="Lemma C.2. ‣ Appendix C Technical Lemmas ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a> and the fact that <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> is executable. In the former distribution, <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> is generated by sampling from <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}(s_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}(s_{h})</annotation></semantics></math>. In the latter distribution, <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> is generated by sampling <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m22" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="s^{\prime}_{h}\sim\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\prime}_{h}\sim\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})</annotation></semantics></math> and then sampling from <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}(s^{\prime}_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}(s^{\prime}_{h})</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, the conditions of <a href="#A5.Thmlemma1" title="Lemma E.1. ‣ E.1 Misspecification Bounds for Composed Policies ‣ Appendix E Omitted Proofs for Expert Distillation ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.1</span></a> are met (after conditioning out <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>), and we get</p>
<table id="A5.Ex163" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex163.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{P}^{\pi\circ_{h}\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}},\mathbb{P}^{\pi\circ_{h+1}\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}})\leq 2\mathbb{E}^{\pi}[\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1}))]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>h</mi></msub><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{P}^{\pi\circ_{h}\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}},\mathbb{P}^{\pi\circ_{h+1}\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}})\leq 2\mathbb{E}^{\pi}[\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1}))]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p4.4" class="ltx_p">as needed.
∎
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We now prove the following restatement of <a href="#S3.Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 3.1 (See ). ‣ 3.2 Errors in POMDPs ‣ 3 Approximate Decodability and Belief Contraction ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmlemma3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmlemma3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma E.3</span></span><span id="A5.Thmlemma3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmlemma3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.Thmlemma3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmlemma3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A5.Thmlemma3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}\in\Pi^{\mathsf{latent}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}\in\Pi^{\mathsf{latent}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a latent (Markovian) policy and let <math id="A5.Thmlemma3.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widetilde{\mathbf{b}}_{1:H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathbf{b}}_{1:H}</annotation></semantics></math> be a collection of functions <math id="A5.Thmlemma3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathbf{b}}_{h}:\mathcal{X}^{h}\times\mathcal{A}^{h-1}\to\Delta(\mathcal{S}_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>h</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathbf{b}}_{h}:\mathcal{X}^{h}\times\mathcal{A}^{h-1}\to\Delta(\mathcal{S}_{h})</annotation></semantics></math>. Define the executable policy <math id="A5.Thmlemma3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex164" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex164.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widetilde{\pi}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1}):=\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}\circ\widetilde{\mathbf{b}}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\pi}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1}):=\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}\circ\widetilde{\mathbf{b}}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmlemma3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmlemma3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex165" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex165.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{P}^{\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}},\mathbb{P}^{\widetilde{\pi}})\leq\sum_{h=1}^{H}\mathbb{E}^{\pi}\left[2\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1}))+\left\lVert\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})-\widetilde{\mathbf{b}}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})\right\rVert_{1}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{P}^{\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}},\mathbb{P}^{\widetilde{\pi}})\leq\sum_{h=1}^{H}\mathbb{E}^{\pi}\left[2\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1}))+\left\lVert\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})-\widetilde{\mathbf{b}}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})\right\rVert_{1}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmlemma3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmlemma3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex166" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex166.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{P}^{\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}},\mathbb{P}^{\widetilde{\pi}})\leq\sum_{h=1}^{H}\mathbb{E}^{\pi}\left[2\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1}))\right]+\mathbb{E}^{\widetilde{\pi}}\left[\left\lVert\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})-\widetilde{\mathbf{b}}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})\right\rVert_{1}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{P}^{\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}},\mathbb{P}^{\widetilde{\pi}})\leq\sum_{h=1}^{H}\mathbb{E}^{\pi}\left[2\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1}))\right]+\mathbb{E}^{\widetilde{\pi}}\left[\left\lVert\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})-\widetilde{\mathbf{b}}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})\right\rVert_{1}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmlemma3.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmlemma3.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A5.Thmlemma3.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1}):=\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}\circ\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1}):=\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}\circ\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof. </span>We can couple <math id="A5.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{\widetilde{\pi}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{\widetilde{\pi}}</annotation></semantics></math> so that at any step <math id="A5.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>, if the trajectories have thus far been the same sequence <math id="A5.SS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})</annotation></semantics></math>, then the probability that they choose different actions <math id="A5.SS1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> is at most</p>
<table id="A5.Ex167" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex167.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left\lVert\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})-\widetilde{\mathbf{b}}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})\right\rVert_{1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lVert\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})-\widetilde{\mathbf{b}}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})\right\rVert_{1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p">By a standard hybrid argument, it follows that</p>
<table id="A5.Ex168" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex168.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{P}^{\pi},\mathbb{P}^{\widetilde{\pi}})\leq\sum_{h=1}^{H}\mathbb{E}^{\pi}\left[\left\lVert\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})-\widetilde{\mathbf{b}}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})\right\rVert_{1}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{P}^{\pi},\mathbb{P}^{\widetilde{\pi}})\leq\sum_{h=1}^{H}\mathbb{E}^{\pi}\left[\left\lVert\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})-\widetilde{\mathbf{b}}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})\right\rVert_{1}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p6.3" class="ltx_p">and also</p>
<table id="A5.Ex169" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex169.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{P}^{\pi},\mathbb{P}^{\widetilde{\pi}})\leq\sum_{h=1}^{H}\mathbb{E}^{\widetilde{\pi}}\left[\left\lVert\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})-\widetilde{\mathbf{b}}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})\right\rVert_{1}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{P}^{\pi},\mathbb{P}^{\widetilde{\pi}})\leq\sum_{h=1}^{H}\mathbb{E}^{\widetilde{\pi}}\left[\left\lVert\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})-\widetilde{\mathbf{b}}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})\right\rVert_{1}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p6.4" class="ltx_p">Combining with <a href="#A5.Thmlemma2" title="Lemma E.2. ‣ E.1 Misspecification Bounds for Composed Policies ‣ Appendix E Omitted Proofs for Expert Distillation ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.2</span></a> completes the proof.
∎
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">The preceding lemma used the intuition that if the latent state is near-deterministic when conditioned on the observation/action history, then resampling it is unlikely to change it. The following lemma uses the intuition that if the <em id="A5.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">action</em> is near-deterministic (which is likely when the action-prediction is small) when conditioned on the action/observation history, then resampling the latent state — and subsequently resampling the action conditioned on this resampled latent state — is unlikely to change the action, though it may have changed the state.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmlemma4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmlemma4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma E.4</span></span><span id="A5.Thmlemma4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmlemma4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.Thmlemma4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmlemma4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A5.Thmlemma4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}\in\Pi^{\mathsf{latent}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}\in\Pi^{\mathsf{latent}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a latent (Markovian) policy and let <math id="A5.Thmlemma4.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widetilde{\mathbf{b}}_{1:H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathbf{b}}_{1:H}</annotation></semantics></math> be a collection of functions <math id="A5.Thmlemma4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathbf{b}}_{h}:\mathcal{X}^{h}\times\mathcal{A}^{h-1}\to\Delta(\mathcal{S}_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>h</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathbf{b}}_{h}:\mathcal{X}^{h}\times\mathcal{A}^{h-1}\to\Delta(\mathcal{S}_{h})</annotation></semantics></math>. Define the executable policy <math id="A5.Thmlemma4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex170" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex170.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widetilde{\pi}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1}):=\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}\circ\widetilde{\mathbf{b}}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\pi}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1}):=\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}\circ\widetilde{\mathbf{b}}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmlemma4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmlemma4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex171" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex171.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{P}^{\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}},\mathbb{P}^{\widetilde{\pi}})\leq\sum_{h=1}^{H}\mathbb{E}^{\pi}\left[2\varepsilon^{\mathsf{act};\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}}_{h}(\pi)+\left\lVert\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}\circ\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})-\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}\circ\widetilde{\mathbf{b}}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})\right\rVert_{1}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>𝖺𝖼𝗍</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{P}^{\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}},\mathbb{P}^{\widetilde{\pi}})\leq\sum_{h=1}^{H}\mathbb{E}^{\pi}\left[2\varepsilon^{\mathsf{act};\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}}_{h}(\pi)+\left\lVert\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}\circ\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})-\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}\circ\widetilde{\mathbf{b}}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})\right\rVert_{1}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmlemma4.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmlemma4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A5.Thmlemma4.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1}):=\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}\circ\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1}):=\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}\circ\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof. </span>As with the proof of <a href="#A5.Thmlemma3" title="Lemma E.3. ‣ E.1 Misspecification Bounds for Composed Policies ‣ Appendix E Omitted Proofs for Expert Distillation ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.3</span></a>, it suffices to show that</p>
<table id="A5.Ex172" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex172.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{P}^{\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}},\mathbb{P}^{\pi})\leq\sum_{h=1}^{H}\mathbb{E}^{\pi}\left[2\varepsilon^{\mathsf{act};\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}}_{h}(\pi)\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>𝖺𝖼𝗍</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{P}^{\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}},\mathbb{P}^{\pi})\leq\sum_{h=1}^{H}\mathbb{E}^{\pi}\left[2\varepsilon^{\mathsf{act};\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}}_{h}(\pi)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p8.2" class="ltx_p">The proof is identical to that of <a href="#A5.Thmlemma3" title="Lemma E.3. ‣ E.1 Misspecification Bounds for Composed Policies ‣ Appendix E Omitted Proofs for Expert Distillation ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.3</span></a> except for using the second claim of <a href="#A5.Thmlemma1" title="Lemma E.1. ‣ E.1 Misspecification Bounds for Composed Policies ‣ Appendix E Omitted Proofs for Expert Distillation ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.1</span></a> instead of the first.
∎
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>Analysis of <math id="A5.SS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{Forward}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝙵𝚘𝚛𝚠𝚊𝚛𝚍</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{Forward}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A5.SS2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-step Executable Policies</h3>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section we describe the (slightly modified) <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{Forward}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝙵𝚘𝚛𝚠𝚊𝚛𝚍</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{Forward}</annotation></semantics></math> imitation learning algorithm <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib62" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ross and Bagnell, 2010</a>)</cite>, applied to the problem of distilling an expert latent policy <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}</annotation></semantics></math> to an <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-step executable policy <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\pi}\in\pi^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}\in\pi^{L}</annotation></semantics></math>. We first formally derive the expression for the policy learned in the infinite-sample limit (<a href="#A5.Thmlemma5" title="Lemma E.5. ‣ 𝙵𝚘𝚛𝚠𝚊𝚛𝚍 with 𝐿-step random actions ‣ E.2 Analysis of 𝙵𝚘𝚛𝚠𝚊𝚛𝚍 for 𝐿-step Executable Policies ‣ Appendix E Omitted Proofs for Expert Distillation ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.5</span></a>), and then prove <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem E.1. ‣ 𝙵𝚘𝚛𝚠𝚊𝚛𝚍 with 𝐿-step random actions ‣ E.2 Analysis of 𝙵𝚘𝚛𝚠𝚊𝚛𝚍 for 𝐿-step Executable Policies ‣ Appendix E Omitted Proofs for Expert Distillation ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.1</span></a> (the regret bound for this policy, restated as <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1 (See ). ‣ 4.1 Theoretical Analysis under Deterministic Dynamics ‣ 4 Distillation is Competitive for Deterministic Dynamics ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>). Finally, we prove a finite-sample guarantee for the modified <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{Forward}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝙵𝚘𝚛𝚠𝚊𝚛𝚍</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{Forward}</annotation></semantics></math> algorithm (<a href="#A5.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem E.2. ‣ E.3 Finite-sample guarantee ‣ Appendix E Omitted Proofs for Expert Distillation ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.2</span></a>), using the same ideas together with a standard finite-sample analysis for Maximum Likelihood Estimation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Foster et al., 2024</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"><math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{Forward}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝙵𝚘𝚛𝚠𝚊𝚛𝚍</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{Forward}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-step random actions</h5>

<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a latent Markovian policy <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}\in\Pi^{\mathsf{latent}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}\in\Pi^{\mathsf{latent}}</annotation></semantics></math> and a parameter <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\in[H]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\in[H]</annotation></semantics></math>, the (modified) <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{Forward}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝙵𝚘𝚛𝚠𝚊𝚛𝚍</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{Forward}</annotation></semantics></math> algorithm computes an <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-step executable policy <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{\pi}=\widehat{\pi}_{1:H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}=\widehat{\pi}_{1:H}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows. For <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=1,\dots,H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=1,\dots,H</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<ol id="A5.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Draw <math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> trajectories <math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tau^{i}=(s_{1:H}^{i},x_{1:H}^{i},a_{1:H}^{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau^{i}=(s_{1:H}^{i},x_{1:H}^{i},a_{1:H}^{i})</annotation></semantics></math> from the policy <math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{\pi}_{1:h-L-1}\circ_{h-L}\Unif(\mathcal{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mi>Unif</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}_{1:h-L-1}\circ_{h-L}\Unif(\mathcal{A})</annotation></semantics></math> (which follows <math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> until step <math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h-L-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h-L-1</annotation></semantics></math> and subsequently plays uniformly random actions).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Compute</p>
<table id="A5.Ex173" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex173.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{\pi}_{h}:=\argmax_{\pi_{h}\in\Pi^{L}_{h}}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\log\pi_{h}(\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}_{h}(s_{h})\mid{}x_{\max(1,h-L+1):h},a_{\max(1,h-L):h-1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>L</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}_{h}:=\argmax_{\pi_{h}\in\Pi^{L}_{h}}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\log\pi_{h}(\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}_{h}(s_{h})\mid{}x_{\max(1,h-L+1):h},a_{\max(1,h-L):h-1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Above, <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi^{L}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>L</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi^{L}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-step conditional distributions <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi_{h}:\mathcal{X}^{h-L+1:h}\times\mathcal{A}^{h-L:h-1}\to\Delta(\mathcal{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{h}:\mathcal{X}^{h-L+1:h}\times\mathcal{A}^{h-L:h-1}\to\Delta(\mathcal{A})</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that the standard <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{Forward}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝙵𝚘𝚛𝚠𝚊𝚛𝚍</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{Forward}</annotation></semantics></math> algorithm is identical except that it draws data from <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{\pi}_{1:h-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}_{1:h-1}</annotation></semantics></math> at step <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>. The modified algorithm is simpler to analyze since the random actions do not bias the conditional distribution of the latent state at step <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> given the partial history <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(x_{h-L+1:h},a_{h-L:h-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{h-L+1:h},a_{h-L:h-1})</annotation></semantics></math>, so this distribution can be directly related to an approximate belief state with appropriate prior (<a href="#A3.Thmlemma3" title="Lemma C.3. ‣ Appendix C Technical Lemmas ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For notational convenience, let <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the policy obtained from the above algorithm in the infinite-sample limit, i.e. at step <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> we define</p>
<table id="A5.Ex174" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex174.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widetilde{\pi}_{h}:=\argmax_{\pi_{h}\in\Pi^{L}_{h}}\mathbb{E}^{\widetilde{\pi}_{1:h-L-1}\circ_{h-L}\Unif(\mathcal{A})}\left[\log\pi_{h}(\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}_{h}(s_{h})\mid{}x_{\max(1,h-L+1):h},a_{\max(1,h-L):h-1})\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>L</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mi>Unif</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\pi}_{h}:=\argmax_{\pi_{h}\in\Pi^{L}_{h}}\mathbb{E}^{\widetilde{\pi}_{1:h-L-1}\circ_{h-L}\Unif(\mathcal{A})}\left[\log\pi_{h}(\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}_{h}(s_{h})\mid{}x_{\max(1,h-L+1):h},a_{\max(1,h-L):h-1})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The following lemma gives a closed-form expression for this policy.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmlemma5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmlemma5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma E.5</span></span><span id="A5.Thmlemma5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmlemma5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.Thmlemma5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmlemma5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">It holds for all <math id="A5.Thmlemma5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in[H]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in[H]</annotation></semantics></math> that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex175" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex175.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widetilde{\pi}_{h}(\cdot\mid{}x_{h-L+1:h},a_{h-L:h-1})=\begin{cases}\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}_{h}\circ\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h}(x_{h-L+1:h},a_{h-L:h-1};d^{\widetilde{\pi}}_{h-L})&amp;\text{ if }h&gt;L\\
\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}_{h}\circ\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})&amp;\text{ otherwise}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>𝐛</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝖺𝗉𝗑</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>d</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>𝐛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> otherwise</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\pi}_{h}(\cdot\mid{}x_{h-L+1:h},a_{h-L:h-1})=\begin{cases}\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}_{h}\circ\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h}(x_{h-L+1:h},a_{h-L:h-1};d^{\widetilde{\pi}}_{h-L})&amp;\text{ if }h&gt;L\\
\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}_{h}\circ\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})&amp;\text{ otherwise}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmlemma5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmlemma5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">so long as <math id="A5.Thmlemma5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> contains this conditional distribution.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof. </span>We have for each <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h&gt;L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h&gt;L</annotation></semantics></math> that</p>
<table id="A5.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex176"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex176.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{\pi}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{\pi}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex176.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\argmax_{\pi_{h}\in\Pi_{h}}\mathbb{E}^{\widetilde{\pi}_{1:h-L-1}\circ_{h-L}\Unif(\mathcal{A})}\left[\log\pi_{h}(\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}_{h}(s_{h})\mid{}x_{h-L+1:h},a_{h-L:h-1})\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mi>Unif</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\argmax_{\pi_{h}\in\Pi_{h}}\mathbb{E}^{\widetilde{\pi}_{1:h-L-1}\circ_{h-L}\Unif(\mathcal{A})}\left[\log\pi_{h}(\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}_{h}(s_{h})\mid{}x_{h-L+1:h},a_{h-L:h-1})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Since population-level maximum likelihood minimizes KL divergence, we get</p>
<table id="A5.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex177"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex177.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{\pi}_{h}(a_{h}\mid{}x_{h-L+1:h},a_{h-L:h-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{\pi}_{h}(a_{h}\mid{}x_{h-L+1:h},a_{h-L:h-1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex177.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{s_{h}\in\mathcal{S}_{h}}\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}_{h}(a_{h}\mid{}s_{h})\cdot\mathbb{P}^{\widetilde{\pi}_{1:h-L-1}\circ_{h-L}\Unif(\mathcal{A})}[s_{h}\mid{}x_{h-L+1:h},a_{h-L:h-1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mi>Unif</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{s_{h}\in\mathcal{S}_{h}}\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}_{h}(a_{h}\mid{}s_{h})\cdot\mathbb{P}^{\widetilde{\pi}_{1:h-L-1}\circ_{h-L}\Unif(\mathcal{A})}[s_{h}\mid{}x_{h-L+1:h},a_{h-L:h-1}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex178"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex178.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{s_{h}\in\mathcal{S}_{h}}\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}_{h}(a_{h}\mid{}s_{h})\cdot\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h}(x_{h-L+1:h},a_{h-L:h-1};d^{\widetilde{\pi}_{1:h-L-1}\circ_{h-L}\Unif(\mathcal{A})}_{h-L})(s_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>𝖺𝗉𝗑</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mi>Unif</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{s_{h}\in\mathcal{S}_{h}}\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}_{h}(a_{h}\mid{}s_{h})\cdot\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h}(x_{h-L+1:h},a_{h-L:h-1};d^{\widetilde{\pi}_{1:h-L-1}\circ_{h-L}\Unif(\mathcal{A})}_{h-L})(s_{h})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex179"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex179.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{s_{h}\in\mathcal{S}_{h}}\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}_{h}(a_{h}\mid{}s_{h})\cdot\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h}(x_{h-L+1:h},a_{h-L:h-1};d^{\widetilde{\pi}}_{h-L})(s_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>𝖺𝗉𝗑</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{s_{h}\in\mathcal{S}_{h}}\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}_{h}(a_{h}\mid{}s_{h})\cdot\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h}(x_{h-L+1:h},a_{h-L:h-1};d^{\widetilde{\pi}}_{h-L})(s_{h})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.3" class="ltx_p">where the second equality uses <a href="#A3.Thmlemma3" title="Lemma C.3. ‣ Appendix C Technical Lemmas ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>. The application of this lemma uses the fact that <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widetilde{\pi}_{1:h-L-1}\circ_{h-L}\Unif(\mathcal{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mi>Unif</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\pi}_{1:h-L-1}\circ_{h-L}\Unif(\mathcal{A})</annotation></semantics></math> plays actions at steps <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h-L,\dots,h-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h-L,\dots,h-1</annotation></semantics></math> that are uniformly random. This proves the lemma in the case <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h&gt;L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h&gt;L</annotation></semantics></math>. The case <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\leq L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\leq L</annotation></semantics></math> is analogous but uses <a href="#A3.Thmlemma2" title="Lemma C.2. ‣ Appendix C Technical Lemmas ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a> instead of <a href="#A3.Thmlemma3" title="Lemma C.3. ‣ Appendix C Technical Lemmas ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>.
∎
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem E.1</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that the POMDP <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>-perturbed Block MDP with deterministic transitions, and fix <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}\in\Pi^{\mathsf{latent}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}\in\Pi^{\mathsf{latent}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a latent (Markovian) policy, and let <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> be the policy computed by <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{Forward}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝙵𝚘𝚛𝚠𝚊𝚛𝚍</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{Forward}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-step random actions, in the infinite-sample limit. Then</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex180" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex180.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\pi^{\mathsf{latent}})-J(\widetilde{\pi})\leq\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{P}^{\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}},\mathbb{P}^{\widetilde{\pi}})\leq O(\delta)+(C_{\ref{thm:belief-contraction}}\delta)^{L/9}SH." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem D.1. ‣ D.1 Belief Contraction ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a></mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\pi^{\mathsf{latent}})-J(\widetilde{\pi})\leq\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{P}^{\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}},\mathbb{P}^{\widetilde{\pi}})\leq O(\delta)+(C_{\ref{thm:belief-contraction}}\delta)^{L/9}SH.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof. </span>Define the executable policy <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1}):=\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}\circ\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1}):=\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}\circ\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})</annotation></semantics></math>. By <a href="#A5.Thmlemma3" title="Lemma E.3. ‣ E.1 Misspecification Bounds for Composed Policies ‣ Appendix E Omitted Proofs for Expert Distillation ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.3</span></a> and the closed-form expression for <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#A5.Thmlemma5" title="Lemma E.5. ‣ 𝙵𝚘𝚛𝚠𝚊𝚛𝚍 with 𝐿-step random actions ‣ E.2 Analysis of 𝙵𝚘𝚛𝚠𝚊𝚛𝚍 for 𝐿-step Executable Policies ‣ Appendix E Omitted Proofs for Expert Distillation ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.5</span></a>), we have</p>
<table id="A5.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex181"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex181.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{P}^{\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}},\mathbb{P}^{\widetilde{\pi}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{P}^{\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}},\mathbb{P}^{\widetilde{\pi}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex181.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{h=1}^{H}\mathbb{E}^{\pi}[2\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1}))]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{h=1}^{H}\mathbb{E}^{\pi}[2\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1}))]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex182"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex182.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad+\sum_{h=L+1}^{H}\mathbb{E}^{\widetilde{\pi}}\left[\left\lVert\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})-\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h}(x_{h-L+1:h},a_{h-L:h-1};d^{\widetilde{\pi}}_{h-L}\right\rVert_{1}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>𝖺𝗉𝗑</mi></msubsup><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad+\sum_{h=L+1}^{H}\mathbb{E}^{\widetilde{\pi}}\left[\left\lVert\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})-\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h}(x_{h-L+1:h},a_{h-L:h-1};d^{\widetilde{\pi}}_{h-L}\right\rVert_{1}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6.2" class="ltx_p">By <a href="#A4.Thmproposition1" title="Proposition D.1. ‣ D.2 Approximate Decodability ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a> and the fact that <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> is executable, the first term can be bounded as</p>
<table id="A5.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex183"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex183.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{h=1}^{H}\mathbb{E}^{\pi}[2\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1}))]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{h=1}^{H}\mathbb{E}^{\pi}[2\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1}))]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex183.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{h=1}^{H}\min\left(\delta,(C_{\ref{prop:vinf-decay}}\delta)^{(h-1)/9}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#A4.Thmproposition1" title="Proposition D.1. ‣ D.2 Approximate Decodability ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a></mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{h=1}^{H}\min\left(\delta,(C_{\ref{prop:vinf-decay}}\delta)^{(h-1)/9}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex184"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex184.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq O(\delta)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq O(\delta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6.3" class="ltx_p">Next, for each <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in\{L+1,\dots,H\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in\{L+1,\dots,H\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can bound</p>
<table id="A5.EGx45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex185"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex185.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}^{\widetilde{\pi}}\left[\left\lVert\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})-\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h}(x_{h-L+1:h},a_{h-L:h-1};d^{\widetilde{\pi}}_{h-L})\right\rVert_{1}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>𝖺𝗉𝗑</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}^{\widetilde{\pi}}\left[\left\lVert\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})-\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h}(x_{h-L+1:h},a_{h-L:h-1};d^{\widetilde{\pi}}_{h-L})\right\rVert_{1}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex186"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex186.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq(C_{\ref{thm:belief-contraction}}\delta)^{L/9}\mathbb{E}^{\widetilde{\pi}}\left[\left\lVert\frac{\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})}{d^{\widetilde{\pi}}_{h-L}}\right\rVert_{\infty}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem D.1. ‣ D.1 Belief Contraction ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a></mtext></msub><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝐛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq(C_{\ref{thm:belief-contraction}}\delta)^{L/9}\mathbb{E}^{\widetilde{\pi}}\left[\left\lVert\frac{\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})}{d^{\widetilde{\pi}}_{h-L}}\right\rVert_{\infty}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex187"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex187.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq(C_{\ref{thm:belief-contraction}}\delta)^{L/9}\mathbb{E}^{\widetilde{\pi}}\left[\sum_{s\in\mathcal{S}_{h}}\frac{\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})(s)}{d^{\widetilde{\pi}}_{h-L}(s)}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem D.1. ‣ D.1 Belief Contraction ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a></mtext></msub><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝐛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq(C_{\ref{thm:belief-contraction}}\delta)^{L/9}\mathbb{E}^{\widetilde{\pi}}\left[\sum_{s\in\mathcal{S}_{h}}\frac{\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})(s)}{d^{\widetilde{\pi}}_{h-L}(s)}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex188"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex188.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=(C_{\ref{thm:belief-contraction}}\delta)^{L/9}\sum_{s\in\mathcal{S}_{h}}\frac{1}{d^{\widetilde{\pi}}_{h-L}(s)}\mathbb{E}^{\widetilde{\pi}}[\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})(s)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem D.1. ‣ D.1 Belief Contraction ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a></mtext></msub><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(C_{\ref{thm:belief-contraction}}\delta)^{L/9}\sum_{s\in\mathcal{S}_{h}}\frac{1}{d^{\widetilde{\pi}}_{h-L}(s)}\mathbb{E}^{\widetilde{\pi}}[\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})(s)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex189"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex189.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=(C_{\ref{thm:belief-contraction}}\delta)^{L/9}\sum_{s\in\mathcal{S}_{h}}\frac{1}{d^{\widetilde{\pi}}_{h-L}(s)}\mathbb{E}^{\widetilde{\pi}}\left[\mathbb{P}^{\widetilde{\pi}}[s_{h}=s\mid{}x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1}]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem D.1. ‣ D.1 Belief Contraction ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a></mtext></msub><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(C_{\ref{thm:belief-contraction}}\delta)^{L/9}\sum_{s\in\mathcal{S}_{h}}\frac{1}{d^{\widetilde{\pi}}_{h-L}(s)}\mathbb{E}^{\widetilde{\pi}}\left[\mathbb{P}^{\widetilde{\pi}}[s_{h}=s\mid{}x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1}]\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex190"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex190.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(C_{\ref{thm:belief-contraction}}\delta)^{L/9}\sum_{s\in\mathcal{S}_{h}}\frac{d^{\widetilde{\pi}}_{h-L}(s)}{d^{\widetilde{\pi}}_{h-L}(s)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem D.1. ‣ D.1 Belief Contraction ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a></mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(C_{\ref{thm:belief-contraction}}\delta)^{L/9}\sum_{s\in\mathcal{S}_{h}}\frac{d^{\widetilde{\pi}}_{h-L}(s)}{d^{\widetilde{\pi}}_{h-L}(s)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex191"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex191.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(C_{\ref{thm:belief-contraction}}\delta)^{L/9}S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem D.1. ‣ D.1 Belief Contraction ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a></mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(C_{\ref{thm:belief-contraction}}\delta)^{L/9}S</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6.4" class="ltx_p">where the first inequality uses <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem D.1. ‣ D.1 Belief Contraction ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a> (and the fact that <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> is an executable policy), and the second equality uses <a href="#A3.Thmlemma2" title="Lemma C.2. ‣ Appendix C Technical Lemmas ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a> (and the fact that <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> is an executable policy). Putting everything together, we get</p>
<table id="A5.Ex192" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex192.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{P}^{\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}},\mathbb{P}^{\widetilde{\pi}})\leq O(\delta)+(C_{\ref{thm:belief-contraction}}\delta)^{L/9}SH" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem D.1. ‣ D.1 Belief Contraction ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a></mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{P}^{\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}},\mathbb{P}^{\widetilde{\pi}})\leq O(\delta)+(C_{\ref{thm:belief-contraction}}\delta)^{L/9}SH</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6.5" class="ltx_p">as claimed.
∎
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.3 </span>Finite-sample guarantee</h3>

<div id="A5.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem E.2</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There is a constant <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\ref{thm:perturbed-mdp-il-finite-sample}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#A5.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem E.2. ‣ E.3 Finite-sample guarantee ‣ Appendix E Omitted Proofs for Expert Distillation ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.2</span></a></mtext></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\ref{thm:perturbed-mdp-il-finite-sample}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> with the following property. Let <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta,\eta,\varepsilon_{\mathsf{opt}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta,\eta,\varepsilon_{\mathsf{opt}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and suppose that the POMDP <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>-perturbed Block MDP with deterministic transitions. If <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq C_{\ref{thm:perturbed-mdp-il-finite-sample}}X^{L}A^{3L+1}H^{2}\varepsilon_{\mathsf{opt}}^{-2}\log(Hn/\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#A5.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem E.2. ‣ E.3 Finite-sample guarantee ‣ Appendix E Omitted Proofs for Expert Distillation ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.2</span></a></mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq C_{\ref{thm:perturbed-mdp-il-finite-sample}}X^{L}A^{3L+1}H^{2}\varepsilon_{\mathsf{opt}}^{-2}\log(Hn/\eta)</annotation></semantics></math>, the output <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> of the modified <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{Forward}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝙵𝚘𝚛𝚠𝚊𝚛𝚍</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{Forward}</annotation></semantics></math> algorithm with <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> samples per step satisfies, with probability at least <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\eta</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex193" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex193.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\pi^{\mathsf{latent}})-J(\widehat{\pi})\leq\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{P}^{\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}},\mathbb{P}^{\widehat{\pi}})\leq O(\delta)+(C_{\ref{thm:belief-contraction}}\delta)^{L/9}SH+\varepsilon_{\mathsf{opt}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem D.1. ‣ D.1 Belief Contraction ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a></mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\pi^{\mathsf{latent}})-J(\widehat{\pi})\leq\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{P}^{\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}},\mathbb{P}^{\widehat{\pi}})\leq O(\delta)+(C_{\ref{thm:belief-contraction}}\delta)^{L/9}SH+\varepsilon_{\mathsf{opt}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover, <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> can be computed in time <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{poly}(n,H,X^{L},A^{L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>poly</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{poly}(n,H,X^{L},A^{L})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof. </span>By a standard analysis of the log-loss for unconstrained distribution classes, <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{\pi}_{h}(x_{\max(1,h-L+1):h},a_{\max(1,h-L):h-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}_{h}(x_{\max(1,h-L+1):h},a_{\max(1,h-L):h-1})</annotation></semantics></math> is precisely the empirical distribution of <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}_{h}(s_{h}^{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}_{h}(s_{h}^{i})</annotation></semantics></math> over the data <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(x^{i}_{\max(1,h-L+1):h},a^{i}_{\max(1,h-L):h-1})=(x_{\max(1,h-L+1):h},a_{\max(1,h-L):h-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x^{i}_{\max(1,h-L+1):h},a^{i}_{\max(1,h-L):h-1})=(x_{\max(1,h-L+1):h},a_{\max(1,h-L):h-1})</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> can be computed in the stated time complexity.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To prove the claimed statistical bound, fix <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in[H]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in[H]</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}=\{g_{\pi_{h}}:\pi_{h}\in\Pi_{h}^{L}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>L</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}=\{g_{\pi_{h}}:\pi_{h}\in\Pi_{h}^{L}\}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the family of distributions indexed by <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{h}^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>L</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{h}^{L}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\pi_{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\pi_{h}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the joint distribution of <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tau_{h}=(x_{\max(1,h-L+1):h},a_{\max(1,h-L):h-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{h}=(x_{\max(1,h-L+1):h},a_{\max(1,h-L):h-1})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{h}(\tau_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{h}(\tau_{h})</annotation></semantics></math> over trajectories drawn from <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{\pi}_{1:h-L-1}\circ_{h-L}\Unif(\mathcal{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mi>Unif</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}_{1:h-L-1}\circ_{h-L}\Unif(\mathcal{A})</annotation></semantics></math>. Also let <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the joint distribution of <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}_{h}(s_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}_{h}(s_{h})</annotation></semantics></math> over trajectories drawn from <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{\pi}_{1:h-L-1}\circ_{h-L}\Unif(\mathcal{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mi>Unif</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}_{1:h-L-1}\circ_{h-L}\Unif(\mathcal{A})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\star}=g_{\widehat{\pi}_{h}^{\star}}\in\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\star}=g_{\widehat{\pi}_{h}^{\star}}\in\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> where</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A5.Ex194" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex194.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{\pi}^{\star}_{h}(\cdot\mid{}x_{h-L+1:h},a_{h-L:h-1})=\begin{cases}\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}_{h}\circ\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h}(x_{h-L+1:h},a_{h-L:h-1};d^{\widehat{\pi}}_{h-L})&amp;\text{ if }h&gt;L\\
\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}_{h}\circ\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})&amp;\text{ otherwise}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>𝐛</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝖺𝗉𝗑</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>d</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext> if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>𝐛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext> otherwise</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}^{\star}_{h}(\cdot\mid{}x_{h-L+1:h},a_{h-L:h-1})=\begin{cases}\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}_{h}\circ\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h}(x_{h-L+1:h},a_{h-L:h-1};d^{\widehat{\pi}}_{h-L})&amp;\text{ if }h&gt;L\\
\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}_{h}\circ\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})&amp;\text{ otherwise}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">by the same argument as in <a href="#A5.Thmlemma5" title="Lemma E.5. ‣ 𝙵𝚘𝚛𝚠𝚊𝚛𝚍 with 𝐿-step random actions ‣ E.2 Analysis of 𝙵𝚘𝚛𝚠𝚊𝚛𝚍 for 𝐿-step Executable Policies ‣ Appendix E Omitted Proofs for Expert Distillation ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.5</span></a>. Moreover, <math id="A5.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\widehat{\pi}_{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\widehat{\pi}_{h}}</annotation></semantics></math> is precisely the Maximum Likelihood Estimation (MLE) estimate over distribution class <math id="A5.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A5.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> samples from <math id="A5.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, we can compare <math id="A5.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\pi}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\pi}^{\star}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}^{\star}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> using a standard analysis for MLE, e.g. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">(<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Foster et al., 2024</a>, Proposition B.1)</cite>: we can bound the log-covering number of <math id="A5.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> (with discretization error <math id="A5.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon:=1/(Hn)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon:=1/(Hn)</annotation></semantics></math>) by <math id="A5.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{L}A^{L+1}\log(1/\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{L}A^{L+1}\log(1/\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>, so we get with probability at least <math id="A5.SS3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\eta/H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\eta/H</annotation></semantics></math> that</p>
<table id="A5.EGx46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex195"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex195.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{TV}(g^{\star},g_{\widehat{\pi}_{h}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{TV}(g^{\star},g_{\widehat{\pi}_{h}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex195.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}^{\widehat{\pi}_{1:h-L-1}\circ_{h-L}\Unif(\mathcal{A})}[\mathsf{TV}(\widehat{\pi}^{\star}_{h}(\cdot\mid{}\tau_{h}),\widehat{\pi}_{h}(\cdot\mid{}\tau_{h})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mi>Unif</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}^{\widehat{\pi}_{1:h-L-1}\circ_{h-L}\Unif(\mathcal{A})}[\mathsf{TV}(\widehat{\pi}^{\star}_{h}(\cdot\mid{}\tau_{h}),\widehat{\pi}_{h}(\cdot\mid{}\tau_{h})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex196"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex196.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathcal{O}\left(\sqrt{\frac{X^{L}A^{L+1}\log(Hn/\eta)}{n}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathcal{O}\left(\sqrt{\frac{X^{L}A^{L+1}\log(Hn/\eta)}{n}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.SS3.p3.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tau_{h}:=(x_{\max(1,h-L+1):h},a_{\max(1,h-L):h-1}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{h}:=(x_{\max(1,h-L+1):h},a_{\max(1,h-L):h-1}))</annotation></semantics></math>. By change-of-measure, it follows that</p>
<table id="A5.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}^{\widehat{\pi}_{1:h-1}}[\mathsf{TV}(\widehat{\pi}^{\star}_{h}(\cdot\mid{}\tau_{h}),\widehat{\pi}_{h}(\cdot\mid{}\tau_{h})]\leq\mathcal{O}\left(A^{L}\cdot\sqrt{\frac{X^{L}A^{L+1}\log(Hn/\eta)}{n}}\right)\leq\frac{\varepsilon_{\mathsf{opt}}}{H}\addcontentsline{lla}{section}{\hbox to20.74pt{\crtrefnumber{eq:opt-error-bound}\hfil}eq:opt-error-bound}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msub><mi>H</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}^{\widehat{\pi}_{1:h-1}}[\mathsf{TV}(\widehat{\pi}^{\star}_{h}(\cdot\mid{}\tau_{h}),\widehat{\pi}_{h}(\cdot\mid{}\tau_{h})]\leq\mathcal{O}\left(A^{L}\cdot\sqrt{\frac{X^{L}A^{L+1}\log(Hn/\eta)}{n}}\right)\leq\frac{\varepsilon_{\mathsf{opt}}}{H}\addcontentsline{lla}{section}{\hbox to20.74pt{\crtrefnumber{eq:opt-error-bound}\hfil}eq:opt-error-bound}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p">where the final inequality holds by the theorem assumption that <math id="A5.SS3.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq C_{\ref{thm:perturbed-mdp-il-finite-sample}}X^{L}A^{3L+1}H^{2}\varepsilon_{\mathsf{opt}}^{-2}\log(Hn/\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#A5.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem E.2. ‣ E.3 Finite-sample guarantee ‣ Appendix E Omitted Proofs for Expert Distillation ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.2</span></a></mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq C_{\ref{thm:perturbed-mdp-il-finite-sample}}X^{L}A^{3L+1}H^{2}\varepsilon_{\mathsf{opt}}^{-2}\log(Hn/\eta)</annotation></semantics></math>, so long as <math id="A5.SS3.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\ref{thm:perturbed-mdp-il-finite-sample}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#A5.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem E.2. ‣ E.3 Finite-sample guarantee ‣ Appendix E Omitted Proofs for Expert Distillation ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.2</span></a></mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\ref{thm:perturbed-mdp-il-finite-sample}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a sufficiently large constant. Next, we observe that</p>
<table id="A5.EGx47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex197"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex197.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{P}^{\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}},\mathbb{P}^{\widehat{\pi}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msup></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{TV}(\mathbb{P}^{\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}},\mathbb{P}^{\widehat{\pi}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex198"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex198.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{h=1}^{H}\mathbb{E}^{\widehat{\pi}}[\mathsf{TV}(\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}_{h}(s_{h}),\widehat{\pi}_{h}(\tau_{h}))]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{h=1}^{H}\mathbb{E}^{\widehat{\pi}}[\mathsf{TV}(\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}_{h}(s_{h}),\widehat{\pi}_{h}(\tau_{h}))]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex199"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex199.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{h=1}^{H}\mathbb{E}^{\widehat{\pi}}[\mathsf{TV}(\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}_{h}(s_{h}),\widehat{\pi}^{\star}_{h}(\tau_{h}))]+\sum_{h=1}^{H}\mathbb{E}^{\widehat{\pi}}[\mathsf{TV}(\widehat{\pi}^{\star}_{h}(\tau_{h}),\widehat{\pi}_{h}(\tau_{h}))]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>𝗅𝖺𝗍𝖾𝗇𝗍</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{h=1}^{H}\mathbb{E}^{\widehat{\pi}}[\mathsf{TV}(\pi^{\mathsf{latent}}_{h}(s_{h}),\widehat{\pi}^{\star}_{h}(\tau_{h}))]+\sum_{h=1}^{H}\mathbb{E}^{\widehat{\pi}}[\mathsf{TV}(\widehat{\pi}^{\star}_{h}(\tau_{h}),\widehat{\pi}_{h}(\tau_{h}))]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex200"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex200.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{h=1}^{H}\mathbb{E}^{\pi}[2\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1}))]+\sum_{h=L+1}^{H}\mathbb{E}^{\widehat{\pi}}\left[\left\lVert\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})-\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h}(x_{h-L+1:h},a_{h-L:h-1};d^{\widehat{\pi}}_{h-L})\right\rVert_{1}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>𝖺𝗉𝗑</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{h=1}^{H}\mathbb{E}^{\pi}[2\mathsf{V}_{\infty}(\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1}))]+\sum_{h=L+1}^{H}\mathbb{E}^{\widehat{\pi}}\left[\left\lVert\mathbf{b}_{h}(x_{1:h},a_{1:h-1})-\mathbf{b}^{\mathsf{apx}}_{h}(x_{h-L+1:h},a_{h-L:h-1};d^{\widehat{\pi}}_{h-L})\right\rVert_{1}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex201"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex201.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad+\sum_{h=1}^{H}\mathbb{E}^{\widehat{\pi}}[\mathsf{TV}(\widehat{\pi}^{\star}_{h}(\tau_{h}),\widehat{\pi}_{h}(\tau_{h}))]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad+\sum_{h=1}^{H}\mathbb{E}^{\widehat{\pi}}[\mathsf{TV}(\widehat{\pi}^{\star}_{h}(\tau_{h}),\widehat{\pi}_{h}(\tau_{h}))]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p3.4" class="ltx_p">where the final inequality is by <a href="#A5.Thmlemma3" title="Lemma E.3. ‣ E.1 Misspecification Bounds for Composed Policies ‣ Appendix E Omitted Proofs for Expert Distillation ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.3</span></a>. As in <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem E.1. ‣ 𝙵𝚘𝚛𝚠𝚊𝚛𝚍 with 𝐿-step random actions ‣ E.2 Analysis of 𝙵𝚘𝚛𝚠𝚊𝚛𝚍 for 𝐿-step Executable Policies ‣ Appendix E Omitted Proofs for Expert Distillation ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.1</span></a>, the first term can be bounded by <math id="A5.SS3.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\delta)</annotation></semantics></math> and the second term can be bounded by <math id="A5.SS3.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(C_{\ref{thm:belief-contraction}}\delta)^{L/9}S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem D.1. ‣ D.1 Belief Contraction ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a></mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(C_{\ref{thm:belief-contraction}}\delta)^{L/9}S</annotation></semantics></math>. By <a href="#A5.E15" title="In E.3 Finite-sample guarantee ‣ Appendix E Omitted Proofs for Expert Distillation ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a> and a union bound over <math id="A5.SS3.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in[H]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in[H]</annotation></semantics></math>, the third term is at most <math id="A5.SS3.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{\mathsf{opt}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{\mathsf{opt}}</annotation></semantics></math> with probability at least <math id="A5.SS3.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\eta</annotation></semantics></math>. Substituting these bounds into the above expression completes the proof.
∎
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Omitted Proofs for Reinforcement Learning</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section we prove <a href="#S3.Thmcorollary1" title="Corollary 3.1 (Informal; see ). ‣ 3.3 The Perturbed Block MDP ‣ 3 Approximate Decodability and Belief Contraction ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Corollary</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, stated formally below.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.Thmcorollary1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A6.Thmcorollary1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary F.1</span></span><span id="A6.Thmcorollary1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A6.Thmcorollary1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.Thmcorollary1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">There is a reinforcement learning algorithm that, for any given <math id="A6.Thmcorollary1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta,\beta\in(0,1/3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta,\beta\in(0,1/3)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.Thmcorollary1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, and any <math id="A6.Thmcorollary1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>-perturbed Block MDP <math id="A6.Thmcorollary1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math>, learns a policy <math id="A6.Thmcorollary1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\mathsf{rl}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝗅</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\mathsf{rl}}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying</p>
<table id="A6.Ex202" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex202.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\pi^{\star})-J(\pi^{\mathsf{rl}})\leq(C_{\ref{thm:belief-contraction-main}}\delta)^{L/18}\cdot\mathrm{poly}(S,X,H)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝗅</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 3.2 (See ). ‣ 3.3 The Perturbed Block MDP ‣ 3 Approximate Decodability and Belief Contraction ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a></mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>18</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>poly</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\pi^{\star})-J(\pi^{\mathsf{rl}})\leq(C_{\ref{thm:belief-contraction-main}}\delta)^{L/18}\cdot\mathrm{poly}(S,X,H)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.Thmcorollary1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">with probability at least <math id="A6.Thmcorollary1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and in time <math id="A6.Thmcorollary1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(XA/\delta)^{\mathcal{O}(L)}\cdot\mathrm{poly}(H,S,\log(1/\beta))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>poly</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(XA/\delta)^{\mathcal{O}(L)}\cdot\mathrm{poly}(H,S,\log(1/\beta))</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof. </span>Recall from <a href="#A4.Thmremark1" title="Remark D.1. ‣ D.1 Belief Contraction ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Remark</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a> that any <math id="A6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>-perturbed Block MDP <math id="A6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-2\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-2\delta)</annotation></semantics></math>-observable (<a href="#A2.Thmdefinition4" title="Definition B.4 (𝛾-observability ( , )). ‣ B.2 Decodability and 𝛾-Observability ‣ Appendix B Additional Preliminaries ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>). Also, by <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem D.1. ‣ D.1 Belief Contraction ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>, <math id="A6.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="A6.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\varepsilon;\phi,L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\varepsilon;\phi,L)</annotation></semantics></math>-belief contraction for any <math id="A6.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A6.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon:=(C_{\ref{thm:belief-contraction}}\delta)^{L/9}\cdot\phi^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem D.1. ‣ D.1 Belief Contraction ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a></mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon:=(C_{\ref{thm:belief-contraction}}\delta)^{L/9}\cdot\phi^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, we can invoke <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem B.1 (( , )). ‣ B.2 Decodability and 𝛾-Observability ‣ Appendix B Additional Preliminaries ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a> with <math id="A6.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma:=1/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma:=1/3</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon:=(C_{\ref{thm:belief-contraction}}\delta)^{L/18}\sqrt{3C^{\star}H^{5}S^{7/2}X^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem D.1. ‣ D.1 Belief Contraction ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a></mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>18</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon:=(C_{\ref{thm:belief-contraction}}\delta)^{L/18}\sqrt{3C^{\star}H^{5}S^{7/2}X^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A6.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> is as defined in <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem B.1 (( , )). ‣ B.2 Decodability and 𝛾-Observability ‣ Appendix B Additional Preliminaries ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>. The choice of <math id="A6.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> in <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem B.1 (( , )). ‣ B.2 Decodability and 𝛾-Observability ‣ Appendix B Additional Preliminaries ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a> indeed satisfies <math id="A6.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon=(C_{\ref{thm:belief-contraction}}\delta)^{L/9}\cdot\phi^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem D.1. ‣ D.1 Belief Contraction ‣ Appendix D Omitted Proofs for Perturbed Block MDP ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a></mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon=(C_{\ref{thm:belief-contraction}}\delta)^{L/9}\cdot\phi^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A6.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="A6.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\varepsilon;\phi,L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\varepsilon;\phi,L)</annotation></semantics></math>-belief contraction, and thus the algorithm <math id="A6.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{BaSeCAMP}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖡𝖺𝖲𝖾𝖢𝖠𝖬𝖯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{BaSeCAMP}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Golowich et al., 2022</a>)</cite> produces an executable policy <math id="A6.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> that satisfies <math id="A6.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\pi^{\star})-J(\widehat{\pi})\leq\varepsilon\cdot\mathrm{poly}(S,X,H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>poly</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\pi^{\star})-J(\widehat{\pi})\leq\varepsilon\cdot\mathrm{poly}(S,X,H)</annotation></semantics></math> in time <math id="A6.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{poly}((AX)^{L},H,S,\varepsilon^{-1},\log(\beta^{-1}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>poly</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{poly}((AX)^{L},H,S,\varepsilon^{-1},\log(\beta^{-1}))</annotation></semantics></math>. Substituting in the choice of <math id="A6.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> completes the proof.
∎
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>A Motivating Toy Model for Smoothing</h2>

<div id="A7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Adding to the discussion from <a href="#S6" title="6 Towards Better Distillation: Imitating a Smoother Expert ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, we informally discuss a theoretical toy model in which smoothing the expert may decrease (a metric version of) action-prediction error and thus improve final performance. Consider a horizon-<math id="A7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> POMDP where the state and action spaces have metrics <math id="A7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{S}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the reward function <math id="A7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> is binary-valued. For each latent state <math id="A7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(s)</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of “good” actions, i.e. <math id="A7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(s):=\{a\in\mathcal{A}:R(s,a)=1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(s):=\{a\in\mathcal{A}:R(s,a)=1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="A7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(s)</annotation></semantics></math> be the diameter of <math id="A7.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(s)</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose that the following natural assumptions hold:</p>
<ol id="A7.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A7.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A7.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The map <math id="A7.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\mapsto G(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\mapsto G(s)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A7.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{S}\to d_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{S}\to d_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> Lipschitz. That is, perturbing <math id="A7.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A7.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> (with respect to metric <math id="A7.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{S}</annotation></semantics></math>) only perturbs the set <math id="A7.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(s)</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A7.I1.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> (with respect to metric <math id="A7.I1.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A7.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Under any observation, the posterior on states is “<math id="A7.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-local” with respect to <math id="A7.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{S}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. contained in an <math id="A7.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-ball.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A7.p1.2" class="ltx_p">With no smoothing, the optimal expert may, for each <math id="A7.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, play an arbitrary action in <math id="A7.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(s)</annotation></semantics></math>, so the “metric” action-prediction error (i.e. expected dispersion of actions played by the expert, conditioned on an observation)
can be as large as <math id="A7.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\varepsilon)+\max_{s}D(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\varepsilon)+\max_{s}D(s)</annotation></semantics></math>. However, suppose the environment has motor noise. In particular, suppose the support of the noise is an <math id="A7.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>-radius ball (with respect to <math id="A7.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>) around the chosen action. Then for each <math id="A7.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, the optimal policy is forced to the “interior” of <math id="A7.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(s)</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. not within <math id="A7.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> of the boundary, effectively equivalent to decreasing the diameter of <math id="A7.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(s)</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A7.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, if <math id="A7.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\gtrsim\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>≳</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\gtrsim\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, then for any two states <math id="A7.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s,s^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s,s^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> in the posterior of observation <math id="A7.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math>, the actions chosen by the optimal policy will lie in both <math id="A7.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(s)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(s^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(s^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, so (under mild additional structural assumptions, e.g. convexity of <math id="A7.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(s)</annotation></semantics></math> in Euclidean space) distillation should produce an optimal policy.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Of course, if <math id="A7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> is too large, the “interior" of some of the <math id="A7.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(s)</annotation></semantics></math> sets becomes empty, i.e. the optimal policy cannot play a robustly good action. As a result, it may play arbitrary actions for these states, so the action prediction error can become large again (and the policy value decreases).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix H </span>Supplemental Materials for Experiments</h2>

<div id="A8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In <a href="#A8.SS1" title="H.1 Misspecification of Decodability in Practice ‣ Appendix H Supplemental Materials for Experiments ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H.1</span></a> we present details for our empirical test of whether perfect decodability holds in image-based locomotion tasks. In <a href="#A8.SS3" title="H.3 Omitted Figures ‣ Appendix H Supplemental Materials for Experiments ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H.3</span></a> we present figures omitted from the main body of the paper. In <a href="#A8.SS4" title="H.4 Experiment Details ‣ Appendix H Supplemental Materials for Experiments ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H.4</span></a> we include hyperparameter choices and details about compute resources.</p>
</div>
<section id="A8.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">H.1 </span>Misspecification of Decodability in Practice</h3>

<figure id="A8.F6" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3"><img src="2510.03207v1/figures/timestep_mse_walker.png" id="A8.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:153/97;" width="153" height="97" alt="Refer to caption"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3"><img src="2510.03207v1/figures/timestep_mse_humanoid.png" id="A8.F6.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:153/97;" width="153" height="97" alt="Refer to caption"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3"><img src="2510.03207v1/figures/timestep_mse_dog.png" id="A8.F6.g3" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:153/97;" width="153" height="97" alt="Refer to caption"></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>Per timestep validation error of the state-prediction model for different choices of frame-stack <math id="A8.F6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\in\{1,2,3,4,5\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\in\{1,2,3,4,5\}</annotation></semantics></math>. The model is trained to predict the state given the most recent <math id="A8.F6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> observations. We present the average error across 5 random seeds.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A8.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each of the three tasks (<span id="A8.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">walker-run</span>, <span id="A8.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">humanoid-walk</span>, and <span id="A8.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">dog-walk</span>), we collect <math id="A8.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2000</annotation></semantics></math> trajectories from the expert latent policy, and for each <math id="A8.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\in\{1,2,3,4,5\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\in\{1,2,3,4,5\}</annotation></semantics></math> we train a model directly mapping from <math id="A8.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> observations <math id="A8.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{h-L+1:h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{h-L+1:h}</annotation></semantics></math> to the state <math id="A8.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, by minimizing mean-squared error. We then evaluate the validation error of the model on <math id="A8.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>100</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100</annotation></semantics></math> trajectories collected from the same policy and plot the per-timestep error in <a href="#A8.F6" title="In H.1 Misspecification of Decodability in Practice ‣ Appendix H Supplemental Materials for Experiments ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>. We normalize the states with the trajectory mean and standard deviation of the combined dataset. Note that the error is composed with three parts: 1) error due to model capacity; 2) using fixed-length frame-stacks instead of the whole history; 3) inherent failure of perfect decodability. We observe that the trained model is able to achieve a small error in the later timesteps, which suggests that error 1, model capacity error, is (likely) small. However, the error is large in the initial timesteps. As error 2 does not exist for steps <math id="A8.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\leq L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\leq L</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that error 3 is non-trivial, i.e., perfect decodability fails.</p>
</div>
<section id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Ablation</h5>

<div id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To investigate whether the error at initial timesteps is due to parameter sharing, we also tried to train non-stationary models (i.e., one model for each timestep) or using weighted loss with higher weights for the initial timesteps, but neither approach significantly changed the results.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Conclusions</h5>

<div id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We conjecture that the higher error at early timesteps is due to a nearly uniform distribution for the initial state distribution, where states that induce occlusion may be quite likely. In later time-steps, the observations along the expert trajectory are in a more stable regime and thus may introduce less occlusion (and hence be more likely to correspond to a unique latent state). Finally, we observe that even at later time-steps there is still significant prediction error. While this could potentially be due to model capacity error, it nevertheless demonstrates impracticality of learning a perfect decoder, and it roughly corresponds with task difficulty (<span id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">humanoid-walk</span> and <span id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">dog-walk</span> are harder than <span id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">walker-run</span>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Source of the error</h5>

<div id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">One may naturally wonder if the error is caused by unpredictable state components that are irrelevant to decision-making (one example could be the absolute position of the agent, but in the environments that we test on, absolute coordinates are actually not part of the latent space). If this is the case, then the error would not negatively impact the performance of the policy distilled from the latent expert.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">One piece of evidence against this hypothesis is that the action-prediction error is indeed non-trivial for our tasks of interest (c.r. <a href="#A8.F9" title="In H.3.2 Action prediction error with smoothed experts ‣ H.3 Omitted Figures ‣ Appendix H Supplemental Materials for Experiments ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>), which suggests that the error is not only due to irrelevant components. In addition, we take a more detailed look at the state prediction error and identify the components that contribute most to the error. With the same setup as in <a href="#A8.F6" title="In H.1 Misspecification of Decodability in Practice ‣ Appendix H Supplemental Materials for Experiments ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, we compute the mean squared error for each coordinate of the state, averaged over the whole trajectories, and present the top 5 and bottom 5 coordinates in <a href="#A8.T1" title="In Source of the error ‣ H.1 Misspecification of Decodability in Practice ‣ Appendix H Supplemental Materials for Experiments ‣ To Distill or Decide? Understanding the Algorithmic Trade-off in Partially Observable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. We see that the coordinates that contribute most to the error are mostly angular velocities of limbs, which are indeed hard to predict from images. On the other hand, the coordinates that contribute least to the error are mostly joint angles or balance point coordinates, which are easier to predict from images. From first principles, all of these coordinates are crucial for the optimal policy, providing additional confirmation that the error is not only due to irrelevant components.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A8.T1" class="ltx_table">

<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>(Left) Top 5 and (right) bottom 5 coordinates contributing to state prediction error.</figcaption><div class="ltx_flex_figure">
